insert into public.school_costs (school_id, academic_year, basis, in_state, out_of_state, source_url, checked, confidence, notes) values
  ('college-of-charleston','2026-27','not-stated','{"total": 35270, "tuition": 12518, "fees": 710, "housing": 15237, "food": null, "books": 1590, "transportation": 2760, "personal": 2365}'::jsonb,'{"total": 63856, "tuition": 39344, "fees": 710, "housing": 15237, "food": null, "books": 1590, "transportation": 4520, "personal": 2365}'::jsonb,'https://charleston.edu/cost-aid/tuition-fees/','2026-10-14','high','Published 2026-27 undergraduate budget assumes 12 credits each semester and includes fall/spring. The single table does not explicitly label an on-campus, off-campus or commuter basis; its room/board explanation uses weighted averages and refers to on-campus residence halls/houses and meal plans. Housing includes food; no separate amounts are printed. Fees are combined technology/athletic/library fees. Both budgets also print $90 loan fees: schema components sum to $35,180/$63,766; including $90 exactly reconciles printed totals $35,270/$63,856. No unexplained remainder. These are institutional average estimates and rates may change; actual housing/meal selections can differ without changing the standard COA. Transportation includes commuting, parking and four annual round trips home. No separate health-insurance amount or alternate undergraduate housing-budget table is printed here. Web fetch failed, so the complete 2026-27 table and definitions were verified in the real cloud browser; the expanded in-state FAQ corroborated all seven costs and total.'),
  ('ithaca-college','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 83020, "tuition": 59440, "fees": 300, "housing": 16520, "food": null, "books": 850, "transportation": 550, "personal": 1100}'::jsonb,'{"total": 83020, "tuition": 59440, "fees": 300, "housing": 16520, "food": null, "books": 850, "transportation": 550, "personal": 1100}'::jsonb,'https://www.ithaca.edu/tuition-financial-aid/undergraduate-tuition-and-fees','2026-10-14','high','Published estimated annual undergraduate COA, full-time 12–18 credits per semester. The college publishes one undergraduate schedule without a state-residency distinction; that schedule is used for both residency fields. Housing field contains combined housing and meals; food is null. Fees field is the $300 Student Support and Technology Fee. Additional health insurance $4,260 is included in the printed COA but can be waived with comparable coverage. Listed fields plus insurance exactly equal $83,020, with no remainder. Books, personal, and transportation are estimates. A separate $325 first-year orientation charge is published but not included in this printed COA. On-campus basis is corroborated by https://www.ithaca.edu/tuition-financial-aid/undergraduate-tuition-and-fees/housing-and-meal-costs : standard double $9,346/year and default residence meal plan $7,174/year match the combined allowance. Alternatives include single/Emerson rooms $10,692, Garden Apartments $11,382, College Circle double $11,666 or single $13,548; upgraded residence meal plans $7,624 or $8,144 annually. Local meal plans are also published, but no alternative full COA total was found.'),
  ('oregon-state-university','2026-27','not-stated','{"total": 38568, "tuition": 16014, "fees": null, "housing": 18066, "food": null, "books": 600, "transportation": 930, "personal": 2958}'::jsonb,'{"total": 65013, "tuition": 42459, "fees": null, "housing": 18066, "food": null, "books": 600, "transportation": 930, "personal": 2958}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.oregonstate.edu/cost-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Corvallis campus 2026-2027 resident/nonresident undergraduate estimates, 3 terms (fall/winter/spring), 15 credits per term. Basis is not-stated because the published living-expense allowance is explicitly an average across BOTH on-campus and off-campus arrangements, rather than a distinct on-campus budget; it applies to students living on campus but only those students are directly billed. Tuition includes fees; housing includes food; separate fee/food amounts are not published in this COA table. Printed components sum exactly to published totals $38,568/$65,013. Billable subtotals $34,080/$60,525 are not COA totals. COA expressly excludes loan-fee allowance, which is added for loan recipients; no amount published. Tuition/fees may vary by program, credits, residency, degree level and final approvals. WUE is a competitively awarded scholarship for limited qualifying students, not an automatic nonresident-tuition reduction. Lower-cost housing options may exist; no alternate on/off-campus COA totals printed.'),
  ('sc-100751','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 700, "fees": null, "food": 5478, "housing": 10000, "personal": 4064, "total": 35392, "transportation": 2352, "tuition": 12718}'::jsonb,'{"books": 700, "fees": null, "food": 5478, "housing": 10000, "personal": 4064, "total": 60400, "transportation": 3354, "tuition": 36724}'::jsonb,'https://afford.ua.edu/cost/','2026-10-14','high','UA ''Afford'' Cost of Attendance page, 2026-2027, On Campus Budget for a full-time, dependent, main-campus undergraduate. Page prints a combined ''Tuition & Fees'' line ($12,718 in-state / $36,724 out-of-state), recorded under tuition; fees null. Personal is the printed ''Miscellaneous'' line. A ''Loan Fee Estimate'' of $80 is printed in both budgets and included in the printed totals; no schema field, noted here.'),
  ('sc-100858','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 18424, "personal": 3088, "total": 39516, "transportation": 3232, "tuition": 13572}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 18424, "personal": 3088, "total": 63540, "transportation": 3232, "tuition": 37596}'::jsonb,'https://auburn.edu/administration/finaid/cost/index.php','2026-10-14','high','Page prints a combined ''Tuition / Fees'' line ($13,572 resident / $37,596 nonresident), recorded under tuition; fees null. Page prints a combined ''Living Expenses (Housing/Food)'' line of $18,424, recorded under housing; food null.'),
  ('sc-104151','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1320, "fees": 2637, "food": null, "housing": 18819, "personal": 2343, "total": 38946, "transportation": 1650, "tuition": 12177}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1320, "fees": 3547, "food": null, "housing": 18819, "personal": 2343, "total": 63394, "transportation": 1650, "tuition": 35715}'::jsonb,'https://admission.asu.edu/cost-aid/resident-first-year','2026-10-14','high','Tempe campus (Campus Immersion) standard undergraduate budgets, 2026-2027, from ASU Admission pages: resident from the source_url page (''2026-2027 expenses for an Arizona resident first-year student''); nonresident from https://admission.asu.edu/cost-aid/non-resident-transfer (same standard budget table). Fees are the printed fee lines summed: resident - Tuition surcharge $350 + Advanced Technology fee $200 + Undergraduate College fee $1,280 + Student initiated fees $807 = $2,637 (the page''s headline ''Resident tuition and fees 2026-2027 $14,814'' confirms tuition + fees); nonresident - $350 + $200 + $2,190 + $807 = $3,547 (headline $39,262 confirms). The Undergraduate College fee varies by program; the pages print the highest possible ($1,280 resident / $2,190 nonresident). ''On-campus housing and food'' is one combined printed line ($18,819, Tempe estimate), recorded under housing with food null. FLAG: a different official ASU page (admission.asu.edu/cost-aid/transfer) prints on-campus housing and food of $15,456 and totals of $35,583 / $60,031 for the same year; the first-year/nonresident pages used here both print $18,819.'),
  ('sc-106397','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1270, "fees": 2580, "food": 5550, "housing": 10144, "personal": 3452, "total": 33988, "transportation": 2656, "tuition": 8336}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1270, "fees": 2580, "food": 5550, "housing": 10144, "personal": 3452, "total": 56256, "transportation": 2656, "tuition": 30604}'::jsonb,'https://finaid.uark.edu/cost-of-attendance.php','2026-10-14','high','Housing is printed as ''Room'' and food as ''Board''. The financial aid COA table''s row for this budget is labeled ''Undergraduate Dep. dorm/off'' - the same budget applies to dorm and off-campus students - so basis is recorded as on-campus. The identical figures appear in the University of Arkansas catalog''s Estimated Expenses table for 2026-27.'),
  ('sc-110592','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 38500, "tuition": 7938, "fees": null, "housing": 13682, "food": 7972, "books": 1128, "transportation": 3002, "personal": 4726}'::jsonb,'{"total": null, "tuition": null, "fees": null, "housing": 13682, "food": 7972, "books": 1128, "transportation": 3002, "personal": 4726}'::jsonb,'https://www.calstatela.edu/financialaid/cost-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Full-time undergraduate, two semesters. Tuition contains combined tuition/mandatory fees; fees cannot be separated from this annual table. Personal maps to miscellaneous. Nonresidents owe an additional $471/unit; no annual nonresident tuition or COA total is printed and neither is calculated here. Shared living/indirect amounts are from the common undergraduate table, which identifies the nonresident surcharge separately. The $38,448 represented component sum plus the separately printed $52 average Direct Loan fee equals $38,500; unexplained remainder $0. Loans fees apply to borrowers and actual fees vary. Alternate CA totals: commuter $29,696 (housing $10,000, food $4,420, transportation $2,096, personal $4,062); off-campus $39,112 (housing $13,604, food $8,662, transportation $3,002, personal $4,726); tuition $7,938, books $1,128 and loan fees $52 apply to each. Both alternate tables sum exactly. Costs are estimates, may change, and vary individually. The Fall 2026 fee page https://www.calstatela.edu/finance-onestop/student-fees lists a voluntary $2 SIRF, $25 late-payment fee, $5 One Card fee and $10 comprehensive-exam fee when applicable. It credits a previously paid $100 enrollment deposit; this is not a discount. WUE-eligible students pay 150% of resident tuition; Fall 2026 full-time WUE tuition $5,128.50 plus campus fees $547.04, without the standard $471/unit surcharge. No WUE annual COA is printed. Case-specific COA increases may cover computers, dependent care, disability, study abroad, cooperative education and required credentials.'),
  ('sc-110635','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 54388, "tuition": 18134, "fees": null, "housing": 23640, "food": null, "books": null, "transportation": null, "personal": null}'::jsonb,'{"total": null, "tuition": null, "fees": null, "housing": null, "food": null, "books": null, "transportation": null, "personal": null}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.berkeley.edu/prospective-students/','2026-10-14','medium','California resident figures, Residence Halls column of the 2026-27 Estimated Costs table: page prints a combined ''Tuition & Fees'' line of $18,134 (recorded under tuition; fees null) and a combined ''Food & Housing'' line of $23,640 (recorded under housing; food null), plus Health Insurance $5,066 (no schema field). The rest of the budget is a single lump line, ''Books, Food & Other'' $7,548, which cannot be split into components, so books, transportation and personal are null. Total Expected Cost $54,388 as printed. Out-of-state: Berkeley publishes no nonresident total - its Student Budgets page states only that new out-of-state students pay additional Nonresident Supplemental Tuition of $39,270 - so all out-of-state fields are null.'),
  ('sc-110662','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1588, "fees": 842, "food": 7568, "housing": 12299, "personal": 2761, "total": 45500, "transportation": 969, "tuition": 15588}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1588, "fees": 842, "food": 7568, "housing": 12299, "personal": 2761, "total": 84770, "transportation": 969, "tuition": 15588}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.ucla.edu/go/coa','2026-10-14','high','Figures are the page''s budget for new undergraduate students starting in 2026-27, On-Campus column. The page prints one combined ''University Fees'' line of $16,430 and breaks it out within the same line as UC Systemwide Tuition $15,588 and Campus fees $842, recorded under tuition and fees respectively. Both printed totals include Health Insurance of $3,885 (waivable; no schema field). The nonresident total of $84,770 is the resident budget plus the printed Nonresident Supplemental Tuition (NRST) line of $39,270; the NRST is not broken into the tuition field, which shows the systemwide tuition charged to all students.'),
  ('sc-110705','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 50946, "tuition": 15588, "fees": 2085, "housing": 13203, "food": 10782, "books": 1515, "transportation": 789, "personal": 2652}'::jsonb,'{"total": 90216, "tuition": null, "fees": 2085, "housing": 13203, "food": 10782, "books": 1515, "transportation": 789, "personal": 2652}'::jsonb,'https://www.finaid.ucsb.edu/costs-estimated-aid/cost-attendance/ucsb-undergraduate-cost-attendance-budget','2026-10-14','high','Incoming 2026 undergraduate cohort in residence halls; nine-month budget. Tuition $15,588 includes the Student Services Fee; fees $2,085 is the separately printed campus-fees line. Nonresident supplemental tuition $39,270 is printed separately from base tuition, so out_of_state.tuition is null rather than an invented combined subtotal. The main table prints resident $50,946 and nonresident $90,216. Resident schema components sum to $46,614; separately printed health-care allowance $4,008, phone $324 and utilities $0 reconcile exactly, remainder $0. The nonresident total reconciles when both printed tuition lines and all other printed categories are included; no loan-fee line is printed. The live official calculator https://finaid.ext-prod.sa.ucsb.edu/costs-estimated-aid/cost-of-attendance/coa-calculator was checked in the cloud browser for 2026-27/Undergraduate/2026 Cohort and confirms the residence-hall budget. Alternate calculator CA/NR totals: private off-campus $46,818/$86,088; university undergraduate apartments $42,843/$82,113; living at home $46,818/$86,088. The calculator currently prints identical private-housing and living-at-home budgets; retained as displayed. All alternate printed lines reconcile with their totals. Budgets exclude winter/spring-break living expenses; estimates and tuition/fees are subject to change. UC SHIP is automatic unless comparable coverage is approved for waiver. The health-cost budget is an allowance, not the exact billed premium; https://studenthealth.sa.ucsb.edu/insurance/uc-ship-academic-year-2025-26 lists 2026-27 undergraduate premiums of $1,336.28 each quarter. Course-material/service, technology and parking charges may apply; a $250 SIR deposit is credited toward registration upon enrollment, per https://catalog.ucsb.edu/academicsandpolicies/studentlife/feesandfinaid/additionalfees. Search-indexed same-year PDF https://www.finaid.ucsb.edu/docs/default-source/default-document-library/2026-2027-undergrad-coa.pdf displays $50,523/$89,793, inconsistent with the current linked HTML and live calculator; PDF direct fetch failed, so those indexed figures were not used. Its alternate indexed location https://finaid.ext-prod.sa.ucsb.edu/sites/default/files/2026-04/2026-2027%20Undergrad%20COA.pdf returned 404.'),
  ('sc-121345','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": null, "fees": 420, "food": null, "housing": 23590, "personal": null, "total": 95670, "transportation": null, "tuition": 71660}'::jsonb,'{"books": null, "fees": 420, "food": null, "housing": 23590, "personal": null, "total": 95670, "transportation": null, "tuition": 71660}'::jsonb,'https://www.pomona.edu/administration/finance-office/tuition-and-costs','2026-10-14','medium','Single tuition rate (private college); the same figures are recorded for in-state and out-of-state. Page prints a combined ''Housing & Food'' line of $23,590, recorded under housing; food left null. The printed Total of $95,670 covers billable costs only (tuition, fees, housing and food). Non-billable ''Travel and Personal'' is printed only as a combined range of $1,500-$2,600, so transportation and personal are null; books are not separately itemized on the page. Medical insurance of $3,312 is listed as an additional cost, not included in the printed total.'),
  ('sc-123961','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 103162, "tuition": 75384, "fees": 1952, "housing": 13510, "food": 8442, "books": 670, "transportation": 1188, "personal": 2016}'::jsonb,'{"total": 103162, "tuition": 75384, "fees": 1952, "housing": 13510, "food": 8442, "books": 670, "transportation": 1188, "personal": 2016}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.usc.edu/undergraduate-financial-aid/cost-of-attendance/','2026-10-14','high','On Campus column of the official 2026-2027 cost-of-attendance table. The page states tuition is the same for California residents and out-of-state students; single rate, same figures in both columns.'),
  ('sc-129020','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 44230, "tuition": 17010, "fees": 4564, "housing": 10186, "food": 6896, "books": 1020, "transportation": 2494, "personal": 1968}'::jsonb,'{"total": 67108, "tuition": 39678, "fees": 4564, "housing": 10186, "food": 6896, "books": 1020, "transportation": 2704, "personal": 1968}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.uconn.edu/cost/','2026-10-14','high','Full-time Storrs undergraduate financial-aid COA estimates, distinct from the page''s initial direct-cost-only table. Both totals additionally include printed loan fees of $92; all printed components reconcile exactly. The published 2026-27 housing estimate explicitly uses average 2025-26 Storrs housing costs; this is the school''s current-year COA figure, not a substituted prior-year budget. Food uses the Value Meal Plan. The separate billing table uses $8,288 standard-double housing and separately lists waivable health insurance and the Husky Book Bundle; those figures were not added to COA. Printed off-campus totals: resident $45,674; nonresident $68,552. For Storrs students living with parents, housing $2,132, food $2,122 and personal $1,288 are printed without a separate total. New England Regional on-campus tuition is $26,028 and COA $53,458. The page also publishes regional-campus budgets.'),
  ('sc-130226','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1100, "fees": 3200, "food": null, "housing": 18440, "personal": 1810, "total": 81830, "transportation": 850, "tuition": 56430}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1100, "fees": 3200, "food": null, "housing": 18440, "personal": 1810, "total": 81830, "transportation": 850, "tuition": 56430}'::jsonb,'https://www.qu.edu/schools/business/programs/bachelors-degree/accounting/tuition-and-financial-aid/','2026-10-14','high','Private university with a single tuition rate; the same printed figures are recorded in both in_state and out_of_state. University-wide ''Full-Time Undergraduate Costs of Attendance 2026-2027'' table (reproduced on qu.edu program pages), ''First-Year Student Living on Campus'' column. Fees are the three printed fee lines: Student Fees $2,140 + Technology Fees $860 + Other fees $200 (orientation fee); the page itself sums Tuition & Fees to $59,630. ''Housing and Food'' is printed as one combined line ($18,440), recorded under housing with food null. The returning-student on-campus column differs slightly (Housing and Food $19,120; total COA $82,310) and is not recorded.'),
  ('sc-130943','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 39154, "tuition": 15740, "fees": 2550, "housing": 9286, "food": 7328, "books": 1250, "transportation": 1000, "personal": 1942}'::jsonb,'{"total": 65884, "tuition": 42470, "fees": 2550, "housing": 9286, "food": 7328, "books": 1250, "transportation": 1000, "personal": 1942}'::jsonb,'https://www.udel.edu/students/student-financial-services/coa/','2026-10-14','high','Newark main-campus budget, full-time enrollment of 12+ credits, fall and spring, standard housing and food. These are estimated educational budgets; actual housing/food selections and programs can differ. Both totals additionally include printed loan fees of $58; all printed components reconcile exactly. Printed off-campus totals: resident $37,214; nonresident $63,944. Commuter totals: resident $27,210; nonresident $53,940. Differential charges apply to Business, Engineering, Music, Honors and Nursing; base figures do not represent these higher-cost programs. For students admitted from fall 2025, annual differentials are Nursing $2,500, Business $3,000, Engineering $4,000, Honors $2,000 and Music $1,250. Separate fee rows list new-student orientation $260 and international-student service $380; neither is included in the selected $2,550 mandatory-fee figure. Continuing-student differential rates also appear.'),
  ('sc-131496','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 100864, "tuition": 74732, "fees": null, "housing": 13944, "food": 8236, "books": 1000, "transportation": 780, "personal": 2132}'::jsonb,'{"total": 100864, "tuition": 74732, "fees": null, "housing": 13944, "food": 8236, "books": 1000, "transportation": 780, "personal": 2132}'::jsonb,'https://finaid.georgetown.edu/aid-for-undergrads','2026-10-14','high','Single tuition rate (private university); the same figures are recorded for in-state and out-of-state. From the ''2026-2027 Annual Cost of Attendance - First Year Undergraduate'' table, ''Living On/Off-Campus'' column (the page budgets on- and off-campus students identically; basis recorded as on-campus). The page prints a combined ''Full Time Tuition & Fees'' line of $74,732, recorded under tuition; fees null. A printed Loan Fees line of $40 (no schema field) is included in the printed total of $100,864. Continuing-student table on the same page: total $101,688 (housing $14,768).'),
  ('sc-132903','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": 6170, "housing": 8750, "personal": 3104, "total": 26272, "transportation": 1094, "tuition": 5954}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": 6170, "housing": 8750, "personal": 3104, "total": 43832, "transportation": 2126, "tuition": 22482}'::jsonb,'https://www.ucf.edu/admissions/undergraduate/tuition-aid/','2026-10-14','high','''2026-27 Annual Cost of Attendance'' for undergraduate students, Fall and Spring 2026-2027, based on 28 credit hours and standard room and dining memberships (recorded as on-campus; UCF''s financial aid office states the same direct costs apply whether the student lives on or off campus). ''Tuition and Fees'' is printed as one combined line ($5,954 Florida resident / $22,482 non-Florida resident), recorded under tuition with fees null.'),
  ('sc-134130','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1220, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 14190, "personal": 2224, "total": 25830, "transportation": 1700, "tuition": 6440}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1220, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 14190, "personal": 2224, "total": 54010, "transportation": 1700, "tuition": 34620}'::jsonb,'https://www.sfa.ufl.edu/cost/undergraduate-costs/','2026-10-14','high','UF Office of Student Financial Aid and Scholarships, 2026-27 Academic Year Undergraduate Cost of Attendance. The page budgets ''On/Off Campus'' identically; recorded as on-campus. Page prints a combined ''Tuition / Fees'' line, recorded under tuition; fees null. ''Living Expenses'' is a combined housing-and-food line, recorded under housing; food null. Personal is the printed ''Miscellaneous Personal Expenses'' line. ''Federal Student Loan Fees'' of $56 are printed and included in the printed Total Budget; no schema field, noted here. Tuition/fee figures are projected estimates for incoming freshmen based on 30 credit hours.'),
  ('sc-135726','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1040, "fees": 2030, "food": 9400, "housing": 16958, "personal": 2294, "total": 98872, "transportation": 800, "tuition": 66312}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1040, "fees": 2030, "food": 9400, "housing": 16958, "personal": 2294, "total": 98872, "transportation": 800, "tuition": 66312}'::jsonb,'https://admissions.miami.edu/undergraduate/financial-aid/cost-of-attendance/index.html','2026-10-14','high','Private university with a single tuition rate; the same printed figures are recorded in both in_state and out_of_state. Food is printed as ''Meals'' ($9,400). The budget also prints Loan Fees of $38, which has no schema field. An international-student total of $104,091 is also published on the same page.'),
  ('sc-139755','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 30928, "tuition": 10618, "fees": 1516, "housing": 8318, "food": 6310, "books": 800, "transportation": 566, "personal": 2800}'::jsonb,'{"total": 55314, "tuition": 34604, "fees": 1516, "housing": 8318, "food": 6310, "books": 800, "transportation": 966, "personal": 2800}'::jsonb,'https://finaid.gatech.edu/costs/undergraduate-costs','2026-10-14','high','From the ''2026-2027 Cost of Attendance'' tables on Georgia Tech''s official Undergraduate Costs page, On Campus Cost columns: the first table set (Georgia resident total $30,928; out-of-state total $55,314). The same page prints a second 2026-2027 table set with a higher Housing Allowance of $10,922 (on-campus totals $33,532 resident and $57,918 nonresident) and a separate out-of-country table (tuition $35,610, total $56,520 on campus); the first, standard set is recorded here. The page also now displays estimated 2027-2028 tables above the 2026-2027 ones.'),
  ('sc-139940','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 34549.51, "tuition": 9270, "fees": 1320, "housing": 11864, "food": 4466, "books": 2066, "transportation": 1037.13, "personal": 4394.38}'::jsonb,'{"total": 56179.51, "tuition": 30900, "fees": 1320, "housing": 11864, "food": 4466, "books": 2066, "transportation": 1037.13, "personal": 4394.38}'::jsonb,'https://sfs.gsu.edu/resources/coa/2026-2027-cost-of-attendance/','2026-10-14','high','Bachelor''s Degree, Georgia Resident and Non-Resident, on-campus columns; excludes Perimeter/associate and out-of-country rates. Published cents cannot be represented as exact integer dollars without rounding: resident total $34,549.51; nonresident total $56,179.51; transportation $1,037.13 and personal expenses $4,394.38 for both. These six fields are null solely because of the integer constraint. Both printed totals equal all printed line items including Direct Loan Fees $132.00, which have no dedicated schema field. Other printed totals: off-campus $37,259.08/$58,889.28 and with relative $28,691.72/$50,321.72 (resident/nonresident). COA is an estimate. The linked overview says budgets cover fall and spring at 12 credits per semester. Totals, transportation and personal were filled from the exact printed amounts in this note.'),
  ('sc-139959','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 978, "fees": 1494, "food": 4718, "housing": 7722, "personal": 3290, "total": 29920, "transportation": 1584, "tuition": 10134}'::jsonb,'{"books": 978, "fees": 1494, "food": 4718, "housing": 7722, "personal": 3290, "total": 52156, "transportation": 2150, "tuition": 31804}'::jsonb,'https://osfa.uga.edu/costs/','2026-10-14','high','Office of Student Financial Aid ''Costs'' page, Undergraduate, Fall 2026 & Spring 2027, On Campus column. Personal is the printed ''Miscellaneous Living Expenses'' line. Off-campus COST OF ATTENDANCE totals are also printed ($29,800 resident / $52,036 nonresident); the on-campus budget is recorded.'),
  ('sc-144050','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1800, "fees": 1995, "food": null, "housing": 21414, "personal": 1950, "total": 103821, "transportation": 702, "tuition": 75960}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1800, "fees": 1995, "food": null, "housing": 21414, "personal": 1950, "total": 103821, "transportation": 702, "tuition": 75960}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.uchicago.edu/undergraduate/how-aid-works/undergraduate-costs/','2026-10-14','high','Verified in the live browser (table not reachable via text fetch). Private university, single rate - same figures in in_state and out_of_state. Fees $1,995 = the two fee lines the page prints separately (Student Services Fee $1,677 + UPASS Fee $318), recorded combined. ''Food & Housing'' printed as one line ($21,414 on-campus) -> under housing, food null. Variants printed on the same table: Commuter total $91,407 (food & housing shown as a $9,000 maintenance allowance), Off-Campus total $100,407 (food & housing $18,000). Footnote: travel allowance varies by state of residence.'),
  ('sc-144892','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 31452, "tuition": 15618, "fees": null, "housing": 13540, "food": null, "books": 150, "transportation": 840, "personal": 1204}'::jsonb,'{"total": 31452, "tuition": 15618, "fees": null, "housing": 13540, "food": null, "books": 150, "transportation": 840, "personal": 1204}'::jsonb,'https://www.eiu.edu/finaid/historical_cost.php','2026-10-14','high','The official Financial Aid Historical Cost of Attendance page includes a current aid-year 26-27 Undergraduate Resident row with a printed full COA total and all components; no prior-year figures used. Tuition contains combined Tuition & Fees $15,618; fees is null. Housing contains Room & Board $13,540; food is null. The official 2026-2027 financial-aid estimate worksheet labels the same $13,540 as On-Campus Living Expenses, confirming the on-campus basis: https://www.eiu.edu/scholarships/docs/2627financialaidestimateworksheet.pdf . Its printed direct subtotal is $29,158 and indirect subtotal $2,294. These are estimates before aid, not guaranteed charges. The published components represented in the schema total $31,352; adding separately printed Loan Fee $100 exactly reconciles to printed total $31,452, with $0 unexplained remainder. Out-of-state domestic values repeat resident values because EIU states that all domestic students residing permanently in the USA qualify for in-state tuition, including a four-year tuition guarantee; the live 2026-2027 undergraduate in-person, 15-credits-per-semester calculator was checked in the cloud browser for both Illinois and non-Illinois residency and showed identical rates. IMPORTANT OFFICIAL-SOURCE DISCREPANCY: https://www.eiu.edu/finaid/cost.php currently prints tuition $10,690.20, fees $4,224.00, combined food/housing All Access Plan $13,670.00 and direct-only ''2026-2027 Cost'' $28,584.20 for 30 annual credits. It provides no numeric indirect allowances beyond loan fees $100. That calculator differs from the coherent full-COA historical table/worksheet set used here, and its direct subtotal is not a full COA. No values were mixed between the conflicting sets. The calculator fees include textbook rental $262.50; this was not added to the separate full-COA Books allowance. International tuition is separately described as 1.25 times the domestic rate; no international amount was substituted. Off-campus/commuter costs are discussed but no complete alternative 2026-27 budget was printed in the selected sources. High confidence follows the printed-total-plus-components criterion; the conflicting official calculator remains an explicit limitation.'),
  ('sc-145637','2026-27','not-stated','{"books": 1200, "fees": 5182, "food": null, "housing": 15858, "personal": 2500, "total": 39380, "transportation": null, "tuition": 15838}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1200, "fees": 5182, "food": null, "housing": 15858, "personal": 2840, "total": 63594, "transportation": null, "tuition": 38514}'::jsonb,'https://fshn.illinois.edu/academics/undergraduate-degrees/dietetics-nutrition/estimated-expenses-didactic-program-dietetics','2026-10-14','medium','The university''s general cost figures are published through the interactive cost.illinois.edu calculator, which a text fetch cannot drive; the table recorded here is the official illinois.edu page (Food Science & Human Nutrition) printing the university''s standard ''Estimated Cost of Attendance for Academic Year 2026-2027''. ''Food & Housing'' is one combined printed line ($15,858), recorded under housing with food null. ''Other'' ($2,500 resident / $2,840 nonresident) is UIUC''s combined allowance that includes transportation, clothing, recreation and other living expenses; recorded under personal with transportation null. FLAG: the printed Illinois Resident total ($39,380) does not equal the sum of its own printed lines ($40,578); the nonresident total ($63,594) does reconcile. Both totals are recorded exactly as printed. Tuition is the base rate; several colleges charge differential tuition above it. The page does not state a living-arrangement basis.'),
  ('sc-147703','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 33872, "tuition": 11010, "fees": 3390, "housing": 15046, "food": null, "books": 632, "transportation": 2160, "personal": 1560}'::jsonb,'{"total": 33872, "tuition": 11010, "fees": 3390, "housing": 15046, "food": null, "books": 632, "transportation": 2160, "personal": 1560}'::jsonb,'https://www.niu.edu/financial-aid/process/costs.shtml','2026-10-14','high','Official 2026-2027 undergraduate full-time academic-year COA, standard non-differential tuition, DeKalb main campus, 12+ credits per semester. The Financial Aid page describes Living Expenses $15,046 as the average on-campus housing allowance including Huskie Block 19 meal plan plus two additional meals per week; the Bursar repeats it explicitly as Housing and food. Combined housing/food is stored in housing, with food null. The schema components total $33,798; adding the separately printed Loan Fees $74 exactly matches printed total $33,872, leaving $0 unexplained remainder. COA is an estimated financial-aid budget, not actual charges; individual expenses vary. In-state and out-of-state domestic amounts are the same: Bursar lists one Domestic Rate and a separate International Rate at https://www.niu.edu/bursar/tuition/undergraduate/index.shtml . Published annual tuition alternatives: Engineering $12,210; Computer Science $11,970; Nursing excluding pre/intended nursing and RN-BS $11,370. Students below 12 credits have reduced COA categories. The COA excludes Student Health Insurance; students with 9+ DeKalb-campus credits are automatically charged unless they obtain a qualifying waiver, and participants can request it be added to COA. Bursar lists health insurance $1,419.50 per fall/spring term, separate from the selected COA. For students living with a parent, printed annual living allowance is $6,688 and travel allowance differs but is not quantified; no alternative total was synthesized. Off-campus allowance covers modest rent, food, utilities and other necessities; no separate numeric off-campus total is printed. Preserve the Financial Aid COA tuition allowance of $11,010 as printed; Bursar separately lists current-cohort domestic full-time billed tuition of $5,505.39 per term and different guaranteed rates for earlier entry cohorts.'),
  ('sc-147767','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1239, "fees": 1260, "food": null, "housing": 22941, "personal": 2079, "total": 99375, "transportation": null, "tuition": 71802}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1239, "fees": 1260, "food": null, "housing": 22941, "personal": 2079, "total": 99375, "transportation": null, "tuition": 71802}'::jsonb,'https://undergradaid.northwestern.edu/how-aid-works/cost-of-attendance/','2026-10-14','high','The page states the same rate applies to in-state and out-of-state students; the same figures are recorded for both. Figures are the page''s Living On-Campus budget. Housing and meals are printed as one combined line, ''Estimated On-Campus Housing and Meals'' of $22,941, recorded under housing; food left null. Transportation is printed as ''varies'', so transportation is null. The printed total includes Loan Fees of $54 (no schema field).'),
  ('sc-151351','2026-27','not-stated','{"total": 30574, "tuition": 12142, "fees": null, "housing": 14398, "food": null, "books": 1320, "transportation": 284, "personal": 2430}'::jsonb,'{"total": 62956, "tuition": 42702, "fees": null, "housing": 14398, "food": null, "books": 1320, "transportation": 2106, "personal": 2430}'::jsonb,'https://www.studentcentral.indiana.edu/cost-of-iu/index.html','2026-10-14','high','Full-time undergraduate, full 2026-27 academic year (fall and spring); tuition allows 40 credits across fall, spring and intersessions. The table does not explicitly label its housing basis or print alternative living-arrangement budgets. Tuition combines tuition and mandatory fees; housing combines housing and food; fees and food are null. Both totals equal printed components. Costs are estimates and vary by student choices, travel habits and academic program. Page still says finalized estimates will be available this summer. Used the explicitly dated 2026-27 undergraduate table; undated image alternative text elsewhere on the same page contains different figures.'),
  ('sc-152080','2026-27','not-stated','{"total": 91986, "tuition": 69280, "fees": 514, "housing": 18992, "food": null, "books": 1250, "transportation": 750, "personal": 1200}'::jsonb,'{"total": 91986, "tuition": 69280, "fees": 514, "housing": 18992, "food": null, "books": 1250, "transportation": 750, "personal": 1200}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.nd.edu/costs-and-affordability/','2026-10-14','high','''Average Cost of Attendance for 2026-2027'' table. Page prints a combined ''Housing and Food'' line of $18,992, recorded under housing; food null. The page does not state a housing basis, so basis is not-stated. Single rate; same figures in both columns.'),
  ('sc-153384','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 93338, "tuition": 73582, "fees": 572, "housing": 8316, "food": 9468, "books": null, "transportation": 300, "personal": 1100}'::jsonb,'{"total": 93338, "tuition": 73582, "fees": 572, "housing": 8316, "food": 9468, "books": null, "transportation": 300, "personal": 1100}'::jsonb,'https://www.grinnell.edu/admission/financial-aid/cost-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Single rate (private college); the same figures are recorded for in-state and out-of-state. ''On Campus - Basic Room'' column of the official 2026-27 Cost of Attendance table. Transportation is printed as ''$300+'' and the total as ''$93,338+''; the printed minimums are recorded - per the page, transportation runs $300-$850 for mainland U.S. students and $1,300 for students from Alaska, Hawaii, U.S. territories or outside the U.S. Books are null because the page states required books and course materials are included in the cost of tuition. Apartment-style housing variant: housing $9,148, total $94,170+.'),
  ('sc-153603','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 26264, "tuition": 9816, "fees": 1586, "housing": 11162, "food": null, "books": 800, "transportation": 450, "personal": 2450}'::jsonb,'{"total": 46762, "tuition": 29864, "fees": 1586, "housing": 11162, "food": null, "books": 800, "transportation": 900, "personal": 2450}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.iastate.edu/getting-started/cost/cost-of-attendance/undergraduate-students/','2026-10-14','high','Fall and spring, full-time 12+ credits, dependent student, ordinary undergraduate tuition. Scripted estimator totals were read in the real cloud browser after selecting each residency; both totals equal printed components. Housing combines housing and food; food is null. Housing uses median campus housing and Cardinal meal plan. Special course fees excluded; some majors and upperclass students have higher tuition. Estimated 2026-27 figures are subject to change. Other displayed scenarios: off-campus dependent housing/food $9,960; independent $12,294; dependent resident with parent $5,305. Independent personal $2,850 and resident on-campus transportation $950; dependent off-campus transportation $950 resident/$1,400 nonresident. International rates are separate.'),
  ('sc-155317','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 33725, "tuition": 11844, "fees": 1065, "housing": 14370, "food": null, "books": 778, "transportation": 2600, "personal": 2962}'::jsonb,'{"total": 53660, "tuition": 31779, "fees": 1065, "housing": 14370, "food": null, "books": 778, "transportation": 2600, "personal": 2962}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.ku.edu/estimated-cost-of-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Estimated academic-year costs based on 30 credits. Housing combines housing and meals; separate food not published. Both totals include a separately printed $106 loan fee, outside the requested component fields; all printed components including this fee sum exactly to each total. Additional course fees excluded. Off-campus totals: resident $32,475, nonresident $52,410; combined housing and meals $13,120, other components unchanged. Financial-aid COA source retained; separate admissions page https://admissions.ku.edu/costs prints differing nonresident tuition and other allowances.'),
  ('sc-157447','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 30958, "tuition": 11328, "fees": null, "housing": 13296, "food": null, "books": 1000, "transportation": 2000, "personal": 2500}'::jsonb,'{"total": 34942, "tuition": 15312, "fees": null, "housing": 13296, "food": null, "books": 1000, "transportation": 2000, "personal": 2500}'::jsonb,'https://www.nku.edu/admissions-aid/financial-aid/tuition-and-fees/2026-2027-cost-of-attendance-6.18.26.pdf','2026-10-14','high','First-year on-campus undergraduate annual budget, main campus; full-time tuition covers 12–16 credits/semester. Tuition stores the printed combined Tuition & Fees; housing stores combined Housing & Food. Separate printed Norse Experience Fee $450 and Student Rec Fee $384 explain the $834 gap between populated fields and each total; all printed components reconcile exactly, with no unexplained remainder. No loan-fee allowance printed. Out-of-state uses the 2NRS new-nonresident tier. Current FAQ explicitly applies the standard rate to all new domestic/international students outside KY/OH/IN; no scholarship condition. New KY/OH/IN students get the same resident rate. Eligibility source: https://www.nku.edu/admissions-aid/financial-aid/tuition-and-fees/tri-state-tuition-faqs/index.html . Current schedule separates students admitted before Fall 2025: https://www.nku.edu/student-account-services/tuition/index.html . PDF also prints a higher Out-of-State first-year on-campus total $42,454 and Tuition & Fees $22,824. Returning on-campus totals: resident $30,508, 2NRS $34,492, older nonresident $42,004. Alternative first-year dependent-undergraduate totals $28,250/$32,234 (resident/2NRS), with housing/food $10,588; self-supporting totals $34,822/$38,806, with personal $6,364. These are financial-aid budgets, not individual bills; program/enrollment and housing choices can vary.'),
  ('sc-160755','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 98710, "tuition": 70622, "fees": 4514, "housing": 11758, "food": 8780, "books": 1200, "transportation": null, "personal": 1778}'::jsonb,'{"total": 98710, "tuition": 70622, "fees": 4514, "housing": 11758, "food": 8780, "books": 1200, "transportation": null, "personal": 1778}'::jsonb,'https://admission.tulane.edu/tuition-aid/cost','2026-10-14','high','Single rate (private university); the same figures are recorded for in-state and out-of-state. Estimated 2026-2027 cost of attendance for first-year undergraduate students living on campus and enrolled full-time in Newcomb-Tulane College. Transportation is printed as ''Varies'', so transportation is null. A printed Loan Fees line of $58 (no schema field) is included in the printed total of $98,710. The page also notes a one-time $300 orientation fee for first-year students among additional expenses not in the total.'),
  ('sc-161004','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 840, "fees": 700, "food": 10326, "housing": 10106, "personal": 1660, "total": 97900, "transportation": null, "tuition": 74268}'::jsonb,'{"books": 840, "fees": 700, "food": 10326, "housing": 10106, "personal": 1660, "total": 97900, "transportation": null, "tuition": 74268}'::jsonb,'https://www.bowdoin.edu/student-aid/cost-of-attendance/index.html','2026-10-14','high','Single tuition rate (private college); the same figures are recorded for in-state and out-of-state. The page prints the total as ''$97,900+''; transportation is printed as ''varies'' (it depends on the student''s permanent residence), so transportation is null and is not a fixed component of the printed total. The standard budget uses the residential 21-meal food plan (food $10,326) and a housing allowance of $10,106. A direct-costs subtotal of $95,400 is also printed.'),
  ('sc-162928','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1377, "fees": 500, "food": 8894, "housing": 13073, "personal": 1606, "total": 94858, "transportation": 738, "tuition": 68670}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1377, "fees": 500, "food": 8894, "housing": 13073, "personal": 1606, "total": 94858, "transportation": 738, "tuition": 68670}'::jsonb,'https://sfs.jhu.edu/cost-tuition/','2026-10-14','high','Single tuition rate (private university); the same figures are recorded for in-state and out-of-state. Figures are the page''s On-Campus Living (Freshman) budget. The $500 Matriculation Fee is a one-time fee, recorded under fees. Student health insurance ($3,624 for 2026-27) is billed separately and is not included in the printed total. The page also prints an On-Campus Living (Sophomore) budget with housing of $14,444 and a total of $95,729.'),
  ('sc-163268','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 42456, "tuition": 14086, "fees": null, "housing": 9248, "food": 6490, "books": 1600, "transportation": 1900, "personal": 7546}'::jsonb,'{"total": 62553, "tuition": 34183, "fees": null, "housing": 9428, "food": 6490, "books": 1600, "transportation": 1900, "personal": 7546}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.umbc.edu/8119-2/','2026-10-14','medium','NOTE FROM CLAUDE: UMBC''s own page lists resident housing $9,248 but non-resident housing $9,428, and the resident line items add to $180 less than the printed resident total $42,456 (looks like a typo on their page; the printed total is used). Annual undergraduate on-campus COA, full-time 12+ credits. Proposed/estimated tuition and fees may change; individual expenses vary. Tuition contains combined Tuition/Fees; fees is null. Personal maps the printed Other category. Printed Direct Loan Fee $142 and PLUS Loan Fee $1,264 are outside the requested component fields. Including both, resident components sum $42,276, leaving an unexplained $180 below printed total $42,456; nonresident components reconcile exactly ($0 remaining). Preserve printed resident housing $9,248 versus nonresident $9,428. Alternative printed totals: living with relatives $33,992/$54,089 (resident/nonresident); off-campus $47,534/$67,631. Relatives nonresident components plus loan fees sum $52,447, leaving $1,642 unexplained; other alternative totals reconcile. Main campus selected, not Shady Grove. The separate semester billing page prints tuition/mandatory fees of $7,050.50 resident and $17,152 nonresident; these differ from the annual COA figures and were not substituted or annualized (https://sbs.umbc.edu/fall-2026-and-spring-2027-undergraduate/). Other fees include undergraduate application $75, enrollment $200, matriculation $100, orientation $225, international $150/semester, and variable course fees (https://sbs.umbc.edu/fall-2026-and-spring-2027-other-fees/).'),
  ('sc-163286','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 34268, "tuition": 11014, "fees": 1820, "housing": 10290, "food": 7180, "books": 1250, "transportation": 1514, "personal": 1200}'::jsonb,'{"total": 65520, "tuition": 42266, "fees": 1820, "housing": 10290, "food": 7180, "books": 1250, "transportation": 1514, "personal": 1200}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.umd.edu/resources-policies/cost-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Estimated annual costs; both component sums equal printed totals. Housing includes cable and phone; food is an average. Off-campus totals: resident $36,066, nonresident $67,318; with-parent totals: $22,752/$54,004. Business, engineering and computer-science majors with 60+ credits incur differential tuition: financial-aid FAQ prints $1,687 per full-time semester; qualifying students may receive an offsetting grant. International students requiring university-issued immigration documents may incur $125 per semester. All charges subject to change. COA source prints resident tuition $11,014; separate 2026-27 catalog https://www.academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/fees-expenses-financial-aid/tuition-fees/ prints $11,015 and annual differential tuition $3,375. COA amounts retained.'),
  ('sc-164924','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1300, "fees": 2074, "food": null, "housing": 19870, "personal": 2000, "total": 100314, "transportation": null, "tuition": 75070}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1300, "fees": 2074, "food": null, "housing": 19870, "personal": 2000, "total": 100314, "transportation": null, "tuition": 75070}'::jsonb,'https://www.bc.edu/bc-web/offices/student-services/financial-aid/undergraduate/how-aid-works.html','2026-10-14','medium','Private university with a single tuition rate; the same printed figures are recorded in both in_state and out_of_state. 2026-27 budget for an incoming student living on campus (meal-plan-required dorm). ''Food and Housing (Living Expenses)'' is a combined printed line ($19,870), recorded under housing; food null. Fees ($2,074) include a one-time $670 orientation fee and a $50 student ID fee for incoming students. The page''s aid-award table prints a combined ''Books/misc.'' line ($3,300); the same page''s indirect-costs table splits it into Books and Supplies $1,300 and Misc./Personal $2,000, which are recorded. Travel is printed only as a range ($150-$1,800), and the page''s footnote states the printed Total ($100,314) excludes travel, so transportation is null. The page also prints Loan Fees of $51, which has no schema field.'),
  ('sc-164988','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 98419, "tuition": 73024, "fees": 1570, "housing": 20740, "food": null, "books": 1000, "transportation": null, "personal": 2085}'::jsonb,'{"total": 98419, "tuition": 73024, "fees": 1570, "housing": 20740, "food": null, "books": 1000, "transportation": null, "personal": 2085}'::jsonb,'http://www.bu.edu/finaid/undergraduate-students/undergraduate/','2026-10-14','high','Resident column of the official 2026/2027 undergraduate cost-of-attendance table. Page prints a combined ''Housing & Food'' line of $20,740, recorded under housing; food null. ''Incidentals'' of $2,085 recorded under personal. Transportation is not printed as a separate line; the printed line items sum to the printed total. Single rate; same figures in both columns.'),
  ('sc-166513','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1200, "fees": 850, "food": 6080, "housing": 11402, "personal": 900, "total": 38402, "transportation": 500, "tuition": 17402}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1200, "fees": 850, "food": 6080, "housing": 11402, "personal": 900, "total": 57610, "transportation": 500, "tuition": 36610}'::jsonb,'https://www.uml.edu/thesolutioncenter/financial-aid/apply/undergrad-coa-odd-year.aspx','2026-10-14','high','Official page: ''Undergraduate Cost of Attendance 2026-2027'', full-time, on-campus columns used. Both budgets also print Loan Fees of $68, which has no schema field. Housing is the page''s weighted average cost (options range $9,990-$13,540). The page also publishes a New England Regional budget (on-campus total $49,158), not recorded here.'),
  ('sc-166683','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 930, "fees": 420, "food": 8104, "housing": 14090, "personal": 2496, "total": 92760, "transportation": null, "tuition": 66720}'::jsonb,'{"books": 930, "fees": 420, "food": 8104, "housing": 14090, "personal": 2496, "total": 92760, "transportation": null, "tuition": 66720}'::jsonb,'https://sfs.mit.edu/undergraduate-students/the-cost-of-attendance/coa/','2026-10-14','high','Private university; charges a single rate regardless of residency, so the same printed figures appear in both columns. Total ($92,760) and all line items are printed on MIT Student Financial Services'' 2026-2027 cost-of-attendance page; the printed components sum exactly to the printed total. Fees are the printed student life fee ($420). Transportation is null because MIT estimates the travel allowance from the student''s home address and explicitly does not include it in this total.'),
  ('sc-168148','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 99998, "tuition": 74862, "fees": 1696, "housing": 11220, "food": 9374, "books": 1000, "transportation": null, "personal": 1846}'::jsonb,'{"total": 99998, "tuition": 74862, "fees": 1696, "housing": 11220, "food": 9374, "books": 1000, "transportation": null, "personal": 1846}'::jsonb,'https://students.tufts.edu/financial-services/undergrad-aid/award-letter/undergraduate-cost-attendance','2026-10-14','medium','On Campus, First-Years budget. Transportation is printed as ''Varies'', so transportation is null. The page prints subtotals of $97,152 (costs paid to the school) and $2,846 (out-of-pocket costs); the total was inferred by adding those two printed subtotals ($99,998). Juniors and seniors have a higher housing figure ($12,588; paid-to-school subtotal $98,520). Single rate; same figures in both columns.'),
  ('sc-168281','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 85600, "tuition": 67000, "fees": 800, "housing": 9800, "food": 8000, "books": null, "transportation": null, "personal": null}'::jsonb,'{"total": 85600, "tuition": 67000, "fees": 800, "housing": 9800, "food": 8000, "books": null, "transportation": null, "personal": null}'::jsonb,'https://wheatoncollege.edu/about-wheaton-college/offices-services/student-financial-services/costs-payments/tuition-and-fee-rates/','2026-10-14','medium','Private college: one rate for all students, so in-state equals out-of-state. Rates page prints Tuition $67,000, Housing $9,800, Meal Plan (Unlimited) $8,000, Student Activity Fee $500 and Technology Fee $300 per year, and a printed TOTAL of $85,600; the companion Costs & Payments page prints the two fees as one combined ''Student Activity and Technology Fees'' line of $800, recorded under fees. The printed $85,600 total is the comprehensive (direct-cost) total: the page estimates indirect costs (books, supplies, personal expenses, travel) at approximately $2,000 per year combined, not itemized, so books, transportation and personal are null. Waivable annual health insurance of $4,939 is not included in the printed total.'),
  ('sc-168342','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": null, "fees": 340, "food": 9490, "housing": 9830, "personal": null, "total": 95960, "transportation": null, "tuition": 76300}'::jsonb,'{"books": null, "fees": 340, "food": 9490, "housing": 9830, "personal": null, "total": 95960, "transportation": null, "tuition": 76300}'::jsonb,'https://www.williams.edu/admission-aid/tuition-aid/','2026-10-14','medium','Single tuition rate (private college); the same figures are recorded for in-state and out-of-state. Figures are the page''s 2026-2027 Comprehensive Fees for the standard residential budget: tuition $76,300, housing $9,830, meals $9,490 (recorded under food), and ''Activities and Residential House Fees'' of $340 (recorded under fees). The printed total of $95,960 is the comprehensive-fee total ''Without Study Away'' and does not include books, transportation or personal expenses; the page text estimates books at $1,000 (not printed as a budget line, so books is null) and prints no transportation or personal figures. A $1,500 Study Away Fee applies as applicable (total with study away $97,460).'),
  ('sc-169248','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 33764, "tuition": 15570, "fees": 450, "housing": 13360, "food": null, "books": 1326, "transportation": 1378, "personal": 1580}'::jsonb,'{"total": 33764, "tuition": 15570, "fees": 450, "housing": 13360, "food": null, "books": 1326, "transportation": 1378, "personal": 1580}'::jsonb,'https://www.cmich.edu/offices-departments/office-scholarships-financial-aid/cost-of-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Mount Pleasant main campus, lower-division undergraduate, fall/spring, 30 credits/year. Estimated costs vary with credits, housing/meal choices, and enrollment duration. Housing contains combined Food and Housing; food is null. Fees are Student Services Fee; books includes course materials, supplies and equipment. Printed Loan Fees $100 are outside the requested fields; adding them reconciles exactly to printed total ($0 remaining). Upper-division on-campus tuition $17,250 and total $35,444; remaining components are unchanged. Alternative lower/upper-division totals: off-campus $29,958/$31,638, with parents $25,395/$27,075. All U.S. residents receive the same tuition; duplicate domestic resident/nonresident values are intentional. Lower division is fewer than 56 credits; upper division is 56+ credits. Standard residence hall and meal plan underpin the housing estimate. Eligible Michigan students may receive CMU Tuition Advantage; no discount deducted (https://www.cmich.edu/undergraduate/cost-aid-scholarships). Separate rate page lists a $5/semester Student Sustainability Fee, not itemized in this COA; it was not added. Military undergraduate rate $250/credit is separate, as are international rates (https://www.cmich.edu/offices-departments/finance-administrative-services/financial-services-reporting/student-account-services-university-billing/tuition-and-fee-rates).'),
  ('sc-169798','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 36572, "tuition": 17352, "fees": 120, "housing": 14748, "food": null, "books": 1000, "transportation": 1260, "personal": 2010}'::jsonb,'{"total": 36572, "tuition": 17352, "fees": 120, "housing": 14748, "food": null, "books": 1000, "transportation": 1260, "personal": 2010}'::jsonb,'https://www.emich.edu/finaid/understanding/costs/index.php','2026-10-14','high','Full-time undergraduate estimate, verified in the real cloud browser after web extraction failed. Resident table explicitly applies to Michigan residents and all domestic undergraduates, so domestic out-of-state uses the same figures. Housing combines housing and food; fees is the printed registration fee. Additional loan fees $82 per residency are included in each total; all printed items plus loan fees sum exactly to $36,572. Domestic alternatives: off-campus $37,584; commuter $25,524. Junior/senior estimated program fees add $2,520, with on-campus total $39,092. International students are the school''s separate non-resident category: on-campus total $37,216, including transportation $1,904. Source conflict: the page retains provisional-tuition wording and registration fee $120, while its linked June 25, 2026 announcement approves a 2.5% tuition increase and a $225/semester Student Services Fee replacing individual fees (https://today.emich.edu/story/story/13343). Published COA table figures preserved without adjustment.'),
  ('sc-170976','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1220, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 17220, "personal": 2458, "total": 40194, "transportation": 400, "tuition": 18896}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1220, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 17220, "personal": 2458, "total": 88394, "transportation": 400, "tuition": 67096}'::jsonb,'http://finaid.umich.edu/getting-started/estimating-costs','2026-10-14','high','Office of Financial Aid ''Estimating Costs'' page, Estimated Fall/Winter 2026-27, Full-Time Undergraduate, Lower Division (0-54 credits) budget recorded. Page prints a combined ''Tuition & Fees'' line, recorded under tuition; fees null. ''Living Expenses'' is a combined housing-and-food line (based on the unlimited basic residential meal plan), recorded under housing; food null. Upper Division (55+ credits) totals are also printed: $42,566 resident / $93,096 nonresident, with Tuition & Fees of $21,268 / $71,798 and identical other lines.'),
  ('sc-171100','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1420, "fees": 466, "food": null, "housing": 13574, "personal": 3930, "total": 38346, "transportation": 1300, "tuition": 17656}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1420, "fees": 466, "food": null, "housing": 13574, "personal": 3930, "total": 67030, "transportation": 2600, "tuition": 45040}'::jsonb,'https://finaid.msu.edu/prospective/getting-started','2026-10-14','high','2026-27 Sample Freshman Budget. The page prints a combined ''Food & Housing'' line ($13,574), recorded under housing; food null. Fees are the printed ''Fees & Taxes'' line ($466). The page prints a ''Personal & Misc.'' line ($3,930), recorded under personal, and a separate ''Travel'' line ($1,300 in-state / $2,600 out-of-state), recorded under transportation; the page text says personal/miscellaneous includes transportation, but both lines are printed, so both are recorded. The page states the same living-cost allowance applies on and off campus; recorded as on-campus.'),
  ('sc-171571','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 35402, "tuition": 16772, "fees": null, "housing": 13326, "food": null, "books": 700, "transportation": 1216, "personal": 3320}'::jsonb,'{"total": 43097, "tuition": 23867, "fees": null, "housing": 13326, "food": null, "books": 700, "transportation": 1816, "personal": 3320}'::jsonb,'https://www.oakland.edu/financialaid/costs/cost-of-attendance/index','2026-10-14','high','General-fees numeric line not printed; fees is null. Fall/winter full-time freshman/sophomore budget (fewer than 56 credits; full-time is 12+ credits per semester). Housing combines living expenses, food and on-campus housing. No general university fees per https://www.oakland.edu/financialaid/costs/tuition-rates/index; separate direct-loan fees $68 and professional licensure/certification/credential $0 are included in each COA. Printed items plus these extras reconcile exactly to $35,402/$43,097. Billable subtotals $30,098/$37,193 are not the COA totals. Alternatives, resident/nonresident: off-campus $35,156/$42,851; with parents $27,928/$35,023. Junior/senior on-campus tuition $18,724/$24,563 and COA $37,354/$43,793. RN-to-BSN on-campus COA $28,625/$29,225. Approved Parent PLUS loans add $248 per semester. Personal allowance includes healthcare. Differential tuition applies in health sciences, business, nursing, engineering/computer science; main estimate is not a program-specific quote.'),
  ('sc-174066','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1000, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 15552, "personal": 2000, "total": 38226, "transportation": 200, "tuition": 19312}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1000, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 15552, "personal": 2000, "total": 63762, "transportation": 1700, "tuition": 43348}'::jsonb,'https://admissions.tc.umn.edu/hs-counselor-guidebook/costs-and-financial-aid','2026-10-14','high','2026-2027 Cost of Attendance, Residence Hall or Apartment budget. The page prints a combined ''Tuition & Fees'' line ($19,312 resident / $43,348 non-resident), recorded under tuition; fees null. The resident column covers Minnesota/Wisconsin/North Dakota/Manitoba reciprocity students. ''Housing & Food'' is a combined printed line ($15,552), recorded under housing; food null. The page also prints a Loan Fee of $162, which has no schema field. A commuter budget (resident total $29,048) is also published; the on-campus budget is recorded. Carlson School of Management / College of Science and Engineering students pay a $3,100/year surcharge not included in the recorded totals (totals with the surcharge: $41,326 resident / $66,862 non-resident).'),
  ('sc-176017','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": 5580, "housing": 8030, "personal": 3500, "total": 32148, "transportation": 3400, "tuition": 10278}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": 5580, "housing": 8030, "personal": 3500, "total": 52938, "transportation": 3400, "tuition": 31068}'::jsonb,'https://olemiss.edu/admissions/cost-of-attendance/','2026-10-14','high','Undergraduate full-time budget with UM-managed (on-campus) housing. The page prints two separate fee lines - Capital Improvements Fee $100 and Student Activity Fee $60 - with no combined fee total, so fees is null and both printed fees are recorded here. The page also prints living-at-home totals of $24,918 / $45,708 and off-campus totals of $36,618 / $57,408. The page does not print an academic-year label; its tuition rate ($428.25 per credit hour for residents) matches the university''s published Fall 2026 tuition, so the budget is recorded as 2026-27.'),
  ('sc-181464','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1128, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 13950, "personal": 2324, "total": 28938, "transportation": null, "tuition": 11472}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1128, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 13950, "personal": 2324, "total": 49008, "transportation": null, "tuition": 31542}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.unl.edu/cost/estimated-cost-attendance/2026-2027/','2026-10-14','high','UNL Office of Scholarships & Financial Aid, ''2026-2027 Estimated Cost of Attendance'', Undergraduate, ''Living On or Off Campus'' budget (the page prints identical figures for on- and off-campus); recorded as on-campus. Page prints a combined ''Tuition & Fees'' line, recorded under tuition; fees null. ''Housing & Food'' is one combined line, recorded under housing; food null. No transportation line is printed in this budget, so transportation is null. ''Loan Fees (if applicable)'' of $64 are printed and included in the printed totals; no schema field, noted here.'),
  ('sc-182670','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1005, "fees": 2426, "food": 8746, "housing": 13032, "personal": 2040, "total": 98946, "transportation": null, "tuition": 71697}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1005, "fees": 2426, "food": 8746, "housing": 13032, "personal": 2040, "total": 98946, "transportation": null, "tuition": 71697}'::jsonb,'https://admissions.dartmouth.edu/estimate-your-cost/cost-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Private university; charges a single rate regardless of residency, so the same printed figures appear in both columns. Total ($98,946) and all line items are printed on Dartmouth''s official 2026-2027 cost-of-attendance page; the printed components sum exactly to the printed total. Personal is the page''s ''Misc.'' allowance. Transportation is null (the page recognizes a minimum $250 travel amount in aid awards but prints no transportation budget line). Per the page''s footnote, a first-year orientation fee of $519 is included in the totals; student health insurance ($5,216 for 2026-27) is NOT included in the total.'),
  ('sc-186131','2026-27','not-stated','{"books": 1050, "fees": 314, "food": 9110, "housing": 13010, "personal": 3000, "total": 94624, "transportation": null, "tuition": 68140}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1050, "fees": 314, "food": 9110, "housing": 13010, "personal": 3000, "total": 94624, "transportation": null, "tuition": 68140}'::jsonb,'https://finaid.princeton.edu/how-aid-works/student-budget','2026-10-14','high','Private university; charges a single rate regardless of residency, so the same printed figures appear in both columns. Figures are Princeton''s standard student budget (its cost of attendance) for 2026-27, First-Year/Sophomore column; total ($94,624) and all line items are printed and sum exactly. Princeton prints different budgets by class year: Junior total $96,034 (food $10,520) and Senior total $96,390 (food $10,520; fees $670). Transportation is null because the page prints it as ''Varies'' (footnote: may range between $50 and $5,000) and excludes it from the total. The Student Health Plan ($4,220 for 2026-27) is not included in the total.'),
  ('sc-190099','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 100224, "tuition": 76828, "fees": 462, "housing": 9348, "food": 10008, "books": 1600, "transportation": 800, "personal": 1128}'::jsonb,'{"total": 100224, "tuition": 76828, "fees": 462, "housing": 9348, "food": 10008, "books": 1600, "transportation": 800, "personal": 1128}'::jsonb,'https://www.colgate.edu/admission-aid/tuition-fees/cost-attendance-2026-27','2026-10-14','high','Single rate (private university); the same figures are recorded for in-state and out-of-state. On-campus ''First-Years & Sophomores'' column. Domestic Travel is printed as ''$800+'' (varies by state of residence); the $800 floor is recorded. The printed Total Cost of Attendance of $100,224 includes an Average Loan Fees line of $50 (no schema field) within the printed non-billed subtotal of $3,578. Juniors & Seniors variant: housing $10,132, total $101,008. A one-time transcript fee of $50 is excluded from the printed total.'),
  ('sc-190150','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 99774, "tuition": 72800, "fees": 4160, "housing": 12522, "food": 7128, "books": 1320, "transportation": null, "personal": 1844}'::jsonb,'{"total": 99774, "tuition": 72800, "fees": 4160, "housing": 12522, "food": 7128, "books": 1320, "transportation": null, "personal": 1844}'::jsonb,'https://cc-seas.financialaid.columbia.edu/eligibility/facts','2026-10-14','high','Columbia College conventional first-year on-campus budget; one schedule without state-residency distinctions. First-years must live on campus. Printed components sum to the printed $99,774 total, remainder $0; variable travel is additional, not zero. Fees include $730 one-time transcript/orientation charges. Continuing on-campus and off-campus totals are $100,884: fees $3,430, housing $13,904, food $7,586; other components unchanged. Living-with-family total $88,060 includes combined food/housing $7,586 and transportation $1,080. Travel examples: Indiana $944, California $1,254, covering two round trips; neither selected. Health insurance excluded: fall $2,218, spring $3,605. Other conditional extras: international services $175/semester, Juilliard $4,600/semester, variable course fees, dependent care. Course-fee waivers generally accompany Columbia grants except physical education. Source comparison: https://bulletin.columbia.edu/columbia-college/fees-expenses-financial-aid/ prints $99,044 plus travel and separately $625 orientation/$105 document fees; its $730 difference is included in the selected first-year table. Bulletin combined room/board $19,650 and books/personal $3,164 reconcile exactly with selected components. Costs before aid.'),
  ('sc-190415','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1234, "fees": 1024, "food": 7604, "housing": 13744, "personal": 2182, "total": 75604, "transportation": null, "tuition": 49816}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1234, "fees": 1024, "food": 7604, "housing": 13744, "personal": 2182, "total": 96140, "transportation": null, "tuition": 70352}'::jsonb,'https://finaid.cornell.edu/cost-to-attend','2026-10-14','high','Verified in the live browser (JS tabbed table a text fetch cannot render). Cornell prints THREE 2026-27 budgets. Recorded here: in_state = NY State Contract Colleges, NY Residents (total $75,604); out_of_state = Endowed Colleges (total $96,140). Third printed budget: Contract Colleges, Non-NY Residents, total $72,504 (tuition as transcribed $47,716, mandatory fees $1,024, housing $13,744, food $7,604, books $1,234, personal $2,182). Disclosure: the nonresident-contract components as transcribed sum to a billed sub-total of $70,088 vs the printed sub-total $69,088 (a $1,000 internal inconsistency); all totals recorded exactly as printed. Transportation printed as ''Varies'' in all three budgets -> null. Books line is ''Books & Course Materials''.'),
  ('sc-193900','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 100998, "tuition": 68576, "fees": null, "housing": 26438, "food": null, "books": 1492, "transportation": 2438, "personal": 2054}'::jsonb,'{"total": 100998, "tuition": 68576, "fees": null, "housing": 26438, "food": null, "books": 1492, "transportation": 2438, "personal": 2054}'::jsonb,'https://bulletins.nyu.edu/nyu/cost-attendance/','2026-10-14','high','Standard undergraduate budget (identical for CAS, Gallatin, Liberal Studies, Nursing, SPS, Silver, Steinhardt and Tandon). Page prints a combined ''Tuition and Fees'' line of $68,576, recorded under tuition; fees null. Page prints a combined ''Food and Housing'' line of $26,438, recorded under housing; food null. The page budgets on-campus and off-campus students identically; basis recorded as on-campus. Single tuition rate (no resident/nonresident split); same figures in both columns. Variants on the same page: Stern School of Business tuition and fees $70,464, total $102,886; Tisch School of the Arts tuition and fees $75,326, total $107,748.'),
  ('sc-196088','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 36530, "tuition": 7070, "fees": 3966, "housing": 10376, "food": 8230, "books": 1500, "transportation": 3078, "personal": 2238}'::jsonb,'{"total": 58530, "tuition": 29070, "fees": 3966, "housing": 10376, "food": 8230, "books": 1500, "transportation": 3078, "personal": 2238}'::jsonb,'https://www.buffalo.edu/financialaid/costs/costs.html','2026-10-14','high','Annual 2026-2027 undergraduate on-campus COA. Financial Aid prints fees separately: Academic Excellence $626, Student Activity $218, Comprehensive $3,122. The $3,966 fees aggregate is explicitly printed by Admissions at https://www.buffalo.edu/admissions/costs/tuition.html, not inferred. Both budgets include an additional $72 Direct Loan origination fee: listed fields total $36,458/$58,458, plus $72 equals printed $36,530/$58,530; no unexplained remainder. Admissions specifies a double-occupancy residence-hall room and Flex 19 meal plan; amounts are estimates subject to change. Off-campus COA is also $36,530/$58,530; living-with-parent COA is $22,698/$44,698 with room $2,550 and meals $2,224. Domestic nonresident figures used; Admissions separately lists international total $61,030 and fees $6,466 including international student fee and SUNY health insurance.'),
  ('sc-198385','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 95195, "tuition": 73090, "fees": 900, "housing": 9220, "food": 9560, "books": 825, "transportation": 200, "personal": 1400}'::jsonb,'{"total": 95195, "tuition": 73090, "fees": 900, "housing": 9220, "food": 9560, "books": 825, "transportation": 200, "personal": 1400}'::jsonb,'https://www.davidson.edu/admission-and-financial-aid/cost-attendance','2026-10-14','medium','Single rate (private college); the same figures are recorded for in-state and out-of-state. First-Year Domestic Student column of the official 2026-2027 Cost of Attendance table. The printed Total Estimated Cost of Attendance is a range, $95,195-$95,595, because transportation is printed as a range ($200-600); the low ends are recorded for total and transportation. Fees of $900 are the sum of two printed fee lines (Required Fees $650 plus the first-year Orientation Fee $250). The printed total excludes the college''s health insurance ($2,800). Returning-student variant on the same page: housing $9,840, total $95,565-$95,965.'),
  ('sc-198419','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 536, "fees": 3019, "food": 10469, "housing": 11560, "personal": 3274, "total": 103180, "transportation": null, "tuition": 73740}'::jsonb,'{"books": 536, "fees": 3019, "food": 10469, "housing": 11560, "personal": 3274, "total": 103180, "transportation": null, "tuition": 73740}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.duke.edu/how-aid-calculated/cost-attendance/','2026-10-14','high','Private university; charges a single rate regardless of residency, so the same printed figures appear in both columns. Figures are Duke''s 2026-2027 estimated cost of attendance for a 1st-year undergraduate student (Karsh Office of Undergraduate Financial Support); all line items are printed. Duke prints the total as a range, $103,180-$103,975, because the transportation allowance varies by home address; the recorded total ($103,180) is the printed low end (transportation at the $582 band). Transportation is recorded as null because Duke prints it only as a range ($582-$1,318 depending on home address). Housing is the double-room rate; food is the first-year dining plan. Not included: Engineering Dues of $60 (Pratt School students only), which account for the top of the billed range. Duke prints a separate returning-student COA of $101,828-$102,623 (fees $2,839; food $9,297).'),
  ('sc-199120','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 28840, "tuition": 7020, "fees": 2130, "housing": 9168, "food": 6702, "books": 638, "transportation": 1078, "personal": 2048}'::jsonb,'{"total": 70264, "tuition": 47472, "fees": 2130, "housing": 9168, "food": 6702, "books": 638, "transportation": 2050, "personal": 2048}'::jsonb,'https://studentaid.unc.edu/current/costs/','2026-10-14','high','From the Office of Scholarships and Student Aid ''Costs'' page, ''26-27'' budgets, Living On Campus columns; a printed Loan Fees line of $56 (no schema field) is included in both printed totals. The page states the in-state budget represents average costs for returning students admitted Fall 2025/Spring 2026: under North Carolina''s fixed-tuition program their tuition stays at $7,020, while new resident students entering fall 2026 pay $7,230 (per UNC''s official Common Data Set 2025-26, section G1, which also prints required fees of $2,129 against the budget''s $2,130, and room of $9,168 and board of $6,702, matching the budget''s housing and food lines). The budget figures are recorded exactly as the student aid office prints them.'),
  ('sc-199139','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 27476, "tuition": 3926, "fees": 3285, "housing": 10200, "food": 5662, "books": 600, "transportation": 1340, "personal": 2360}'::jsonb,'{"total": 46228, "tuition": 22018, "fees": 3285, "housing": 10200, "food": 5662, "books": 600, "transportation": 2000, "personal": 2360}'::jsonb,'https://admissions.charlotte.edu/financing-your-education/cost-of-attendance/','2026-10-14','high','Official admissions full-year, full-time undergraduate on-campus estimate for NC residents/nonresidents. Additional printed loan fees $103 for each residency are included in the COA; listed fields plus loan fees sum exactly to $27,476/$46,228. Nonresident Miscellaneous is mapped to personal. All costs are identified as subject to change pending legislative approval. Financial-aid/Niner Central estimating-costs page was checked first but live web/browser retrieval failed with 502 certificate verification error; indexed financial-aid content showed earlier years only and was not substituted. On-campus 2026-27 values are directly printed on admissions. Health insurance has no amount in this budget; no amount added. Off-campus/at-home budgets are linked to Niner Central but not verified for 2026-27.'),
  ('sc-199847','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": null, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": null, "personal": null, "total": 98730, "transportation": null, "tuition": null}'::jsonb,'{"books": null, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": null, "personal": null, "total": 98730, "transportation": null, "tuition": null}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.wfu.edu/cost-of-attendance','2026-10-14','medium','Private university with a single tuition rate; the same printed figure is recorded in both in_state and out_of_state. The Student Financial Aid page prints only the total for 2026-27: ''Living on or off campus - Total Estimated Costs: $98,730'' (one identical budget for on- and off-campus living, recorded as on-campus per program rules); its line-item breakdown did not render in a text fetch, so all line items are null. A ''Living with parents'' total of $84,674 is also published. Per the page, standard student fees are Activity, Wellness, and Health Service; a $380 Orientation Fee is additionally assessed in a new student''s first semester; the estimate excludes health insurance.'),
  ('sc-200004','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 22906.82, "tuition": 4598, "fees": null, "housing": 7233.74, "food": 5799.4, "books": 406.74, "transportation": 1885.14, "personal": 1686.9}'::jsonb,'{"total": 28906.82, "tuition": 10598, "fees": null, "housing": 7233.74, "food": 5799.4, "books": 406.74, "transportation": 1885.14, "personal": 1686.9}'::jsonb,'https://www.wcu.edu/apply/financial-aid/COA.aspx','2026-10-14','high','Financial-aid COA for full-time undergraduate enrollment, 12+ credits; housing allowance is explicitly based on on-campus costs. Tuition field contains published combined tuition and fees; separate fees not published. Extra published lines: loan fees $77 and new-student computer $1,219.90, for each residency. Listed fields plus those extras exactly equal each printed total, with no remainder. Computer allowance applies automatically to new students; continuing students can request it after 3+ years. Off-campus housing may be reviewed individually. Distance-education undergraduate alternative totals are $23,223.54 resident and $29,223.46 nonresident; not mixed into this record. Source conflict/context: https://www.wcu.edu/apply/tuition-and-fees/fall-spring-undergraduate-tuition-and-fees.aspx publishes per-semester tuition/fees $3,690 resident, $6,690 new AY26-27 nonresident, and $5,690 continuing AY25-26 nonresident, including $1,312 waivable health insurance per semester. Those billing figures do not directly match the COA tuition/fees line; the financial-aid COA was retained unchanged. NC Promise cohort pricing and proposal/change caveats apply. Residence-hall technology fee is $92 per semester; program-specific fees and parking can add costs. Billing-page sample totals are semester direct costs, not annual COA.'),
  ('sc-204796','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1020, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 15630, "personal": 2686, "total": 34142, "transportation": 732, "tuition": 14034}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1020, "fees": 30220, "food": null, "housing": 15630, "personal": 2686, "total": 64990, "transportation": 1360, "tuition": 14034}'::jsonb,'http://sfa.osu.edu/incoming-freshmen/about-aid/financial-aid-eligibility','2026-10-14','high','Student Financial Aid ''Cost and aid eligibility'' page, Incoming Freshmen, Cost of Attendance 2026-2027 Academic Year, Columbus campus, living on campus. Page prints a combined ''Tuition and fees'' line of $14,034, recorded under tuition; in-state fees null. The nonresident budget adds a separate printed ''Non-resident fees'' line of $30,220, recorded under fees. ''Living expenses: housing and food'' is printed as one combined line of $15,630, recorded under housing; food null. ''Federal student loan fees'' of $40 are printed and included in the printed totals; no schema field, noted here. Page also prints a resident off-campus total of $33,322 and a commuter total of $26,494.'),
  ('sc-207388','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 34590, "tuition": 14740, "fees": null, "housing": 12500, "food": null, "books": 1430, "transportation": 2350, "personal": 3570}'::jsonb,'{"total": 50850, "tuition": 31000, "fees": null, "housing": 12500, "food": null, "books": 1430, "transportation": 2350, "personal": 3570}'::jsonb,'https://go.okstate.edu/scholarships-financial-aid/cost-of-attendance/undergraduate-cost/in-state-cost/previous-year-cost','2026-10-14','medium','NOTE FROM CLAUDE: Oklahoma State''s own PDF worksheets print a different on-campus total ($33,700 / $49,220) than the dated web tables used here; medium confidence until they agree. August 2026-May 2027 undergraduate estimates, 30 credit hours, Stillwater main campus. Tuition contains published combined tuition-and-fees; fees is null. Housing contains published combined housing-and-food; food is null. In-state evidence: https://go.okstate.edu/scholarships-financial-aid/cost-of-attendance/undergraduate-cost/in-state-cost/previous-year-cost. Nonresident evidence: https://go.okstate.edu/scholarships-financial-aid/cost-of-attendance/undergraduate-cost/out-of-state-cost/previous-year-cost. The Financial Aid hub offers both 2027-2028 and 2026-2027 links. Its 2026-2027 links lead to these previous-year-cost URLs, whose headings and August 2026-May 2027 date ranges explicitly match the requested year; no 2027-2028 amounts are used. Printed line items sum exactly to $34,590/$50,850; no separately listed loan/insurance allowance or unexplained remainder. Direct subtotals $28,670/$44,930 are not COA totals. Alternative totals: off-campus $35,330/$51,590; commuter $30,800/$47,060; on-campus with dependents $35,120/$51,380. Source conflict: 2026-27 PDF worksheets instead print tuition/fees $13,920/$29,440, personal $3,500, and on-campus COA $33,700/$49,220. Selected the explicitly year-labeled HTML tables linked under 2026-2027 by Financial Aid; relative revision timing versus the worksheets is not verified. The contradictory PDF figures are preserved here and are not mixed with the selected HTML figures. Conflicting PDFs: https://go.okstate.edu/scholarships-financial-aid/files/documents/26-27/info-sheets/college_cost_worksheet_in_state_2026_2027.pdf and https://go.okstate.edu/scholarships-financial-aid/files/documents/26-27/info-sheets/college_cost_worksheet_out_of_state_2026_2027.pdf.'),
  ('sc-207500','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 40145, "tuition": 5532, "fees": 9971, "housing": 16381, "food": null, "books": 800, "transportation": 1728, "personal": 5665}'::jsonb,'{"total": 58823, "tuition": 24210, "fees": 9971, "housing": 16381, "food": null, "books": 800, "transportation": 1728, "personal": 5665}'::jsonb,'https://www.ou.edu/sfc/estimating-costs/cost-of-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Published 2026-2027 fall/spring, 30-credit estimate for incoming first-year students. Housing includes food; no separate food amount. Both residency tables also print $68 loan fees: displayed schema components sum to $40,077/$58,755, and adding $68 exactly reconciles the published $40,145/$58,823 totals. Direct-cost subtotals $32,684/$51,362 are not COA totals. Alternatives: on-campus with children totals $37,900/$56,578 (housing/food $14,136); off-campus totals $37,918/$56,596 (housing/food $14,154). Tuition/fees vary by courses; full-time flat rate covers 12–21 hours per semester at the 15-hour rate. Aviation flying majors have estimated additional tuition/fees $15,000 annually; specified architecture/art/engineering/computer-science/petroleum-engineering students have estimated additional one-time laptop cost $2,000. Separate international budget includes medical insurance $2,795 and $154 annual international maintenance fee; not applied to domestic nonresidents. Admissions page https://www.ou.edu/admissions/affordability/cost corroborates selected amounts. No unexplained total remainder.'),
  ('sc-211440','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 93614, "tuition": 69702, "fees": 1862, "housing": 11700, "food": 7950, "books": 1000, "transportation": 0, "personal": 1300}'::jsonb,'{"total": 93614, "tuition": 69702, "fees": 1862, "housing": 11700, "food": 7950, "books": 1000, "transportation": 0, "personal": 1300}'::jsonb,'http://coursecatalog.web.cmu.edu/aboutcmu/costofattendance/','2026-10-14','medium','''First-Years Entering Fall 2026'', Resident column. Transportation Allowance is printed as $0. Fees are the sum of four printed fee lines (First-Year Experience Fee $748, Technology Fee $490, Student Activities Fee $322, Transportation Fee $302 = $1,862), so fees were inferred by adding printed lines. The printed total also includes an Estimated Loan Fees line of $100 (no schema field). Continuing students (entered 2025 and earlier) have different figures: housing $14,940 and total $96,106. Single rate; same figures in both columns.'),
  ('sc-216287','2026-27','not-stated','{"books": 825, "fees": 482, "food": 10890, "housing": 11676, "personal": 1775, "total": 98370, "transportation": null, "tuition": 72722}'::jsonb,'{"books": 825, "fees": 482, "food": 10890, "housing": 11676, "personal": 1775, "total": 98370, "transportation": null, "tuition": 72722}'::jsonb,'http://www.swarthmore.edu/financial-aid/tuition-books-housing-food-plan-activities-fee','2026-10-14','high','Single tuition rate (private college); the same figures are recorded for in-state and out-of-state. The billed charge is printed as a combined ''Tuition and Books'' line of $72,722, recorded under tuition; the page notes tuition includes an $800 Textbook Affordability Program credit toward course materials. Separately, the page prints a non-billed ''Course materials, supplies and equipment'' allowance of $825, recorded under books. Fees are the Student Activities Fee of $482. The page also prints Total Billed Charges of $95,770; the printed Total Cost of Attendance of $98,370 adds the course-materials and personal-expense allowances. Transportation is printed as ''Varies'', so transportation is null.'),
  ('sc-216597','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 600, "fees": 1024, "food": 9040, "housing": 10314, "personal": 1450, "total": 96886, "transportation": 850, "tuition": 72990}'::jsonb,'{"books": 600, "fees": 1024, "food": 9040, "housing": 10314, "personal": 1450, "total": 96886, "transportation": 850, "tuition": 72990}'::jsonb,'http://www.villanova.edu/university/office-of-financial-assistance/financial-aid-process/cost-of-attendance.html','2026-10-14','high','Private university with a single tuition rate; the same printed figures are recorded in both in_state and out_of_state. Fees are the printed ''Student Services Fee'' ($1,024) and food is printed as ''Food/Meals'' ($9,040). Supplies of $560 (freshman figure; $160 for returning students) and Loan Fees of $58 are printed but have no schema field. A commuter budget with a total of $80,652 is also printed on the page. The page notes health insurance of approximately $3,165 per year is not included in the cost of attendance.'),
  ('sc-217156','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": null, "fees": 3084, "food": 8754, "housing": 10710, "personal": 2878, "total": 99994, "transportation": null, "tuition": 74568}'::jsonb,'{"books": null, "fees": 3084, "food": 8754, "housing": 10710, "personal": 2878, "total": 99994, "transportation": null, "tuition": 74568}'::jsonb,'https://finaid.brown.edu/estimate-cost-aid/cost','2026-10-14','high','Private university; charges a single rate regardless of residency, so the same printed figures appear in both columns. Total ($99,994) and all line items are printed on Brown''s Office of Financial Aid cost-of-attendance page; the identical charges are labeled 2026-2027 on Brown''s Student Financial Services tuition page. Fees ($3,084) include the $100 one-time Academic Record Fee charged to first-time students. Brown publishes the same total for full-time off-campus students. Books are null because Brown does not include a books component in the standard COA (the Book/Course Material Support program covers books for scholarship-eligible students; a standard $1,300 books allowance applies only to students outside that program and is not in the printed total; supply costs are folded into personal expenses). Transportation is null because Brown adds a travel allowance based on the student''s home address, with no standard figure in the printed total. The Student Health Insurance Plan ($5,283 for 2026-27) is not included unless a student does not waive it.'),
  ('sc-217882','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 40722, "tuition": 14038, "fees": 1832, "housing": 9304, "food": 5576, "books": 1576, "transportation": 1320, "personal": 4484}'::jsonb,'{"total": 68704, "tuition": 42020, "fees": 1832, "housing": 9304, "food": 5576, "books": 1576, "transportation": 1320, "personal": 4484}'::jsonb,'https://www.clemson.edu/financial-aid/cost/estimated-cost-of-attendance.html','2026-10-14','high','Fall/spring full-time estimates; shared on/off-campus column uses average dormitory and unlimited meal plan. Incoming-first-year basis selects the explicitly printed totals with laptop: $40,722/$68,704. Extras included: $2,524 first-year laptop and $68 average federal Direct Loan fees if applicable. Base printed totals without laptop are $38,198/$66,180. Major enrichment $0-$2,500 is excluded; no endpoint selected. Fees cover mandatory and average laboratory fees. Listed components plus loan/laptop extras reconcile exactly; no unexplained remainder. Commuter housing/food each $2,023; transportation $3,672; totals $29,716/$57,698 or $32,240/$60,222 with laptop. Additional source https://www.clemson.edu/admissions/undergraduate-admissions/afford.html describes health fees and shows conflicting nonresident tuition/fees $42,852, versus primary tuition $42,020 plus fees $1,832. Its $60,308 partial total exceeds its own listed components by $1,000; primary figures retained.'),
  ('sc-218663','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 40584, "tuition": 12288, "fees": 400, "housing": 11432, "food": 5902, "books": 1522, "transportation": 2670, "personal": 4790}'::jsonb,'{"total": 66394, "tuition": 38098, "fees": 400, "housing": 11432, "food": 5902, "books": 1522, "transportation": 2670, "personal": 4790}'::jsonb,'https://sc.edu/about/offices_and_divisions/financial_aid/cost_and_aid/cost_to_attend/','2026-10-14','high','Conventional undergraduate, fall/spring, 12 credits per term, on-campus column. Fees field is the printed $400 Tech Fee only. Additional printed $1,580 weighted-average program fees apply to both residencies and are included in totals. Components plus that extra reconcile exactly to $40,584/$66,394; no unexplained remainder. Estimates vary by major and personal choices. Off-campus printed totals are also $40,584/$66,394; with-parent housing $2,630 and totals $31,782/$57,592. Nonresident off-campus/with-parent transportation is printed $2,690 versus on-campus $2,670; those alternate component sums exceed their printed totals by $20. Resident off-campus housing is printed with a semicolon ($11;432); the on-campus value is unambiguous. No separate undergraduate loan fee or health-insurance amount is printed.'),
  ('sc-221759','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1598, "fees": 2464, "food": 5166, "housing": 9572, "personal": 3042, "total": 36994, "transportation": 3500, "tuition": 11560}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1598, "fees": 2806, "food": 5166, "housing": 9572, "personal": 3042, "total": 57448, "transportation": 3500, "tuition": 31672}'::jsonb,'https://onestop.utk.edu/billing-payments/cost-of-attending-ut-undergraduate-student/','2026-10-14','high','On-campus undergraduate budget. The page also prints Loan Fees of $92, which has no schema field, and off-campus totals of $39,494 (in-state) / $58,938 (out-of-state).'),
  ('sc-228246','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 888, "fees": 8080, "food": null, "housing": 20950, "personal": 1600, "total": 96388, "transportation": 1134, "tuition": 63736}'::jsonb,'{"books": 888, "fees": 8080, "food": null, "housing": 20950, "personal": 1600, "total": 96388, "transportation": 1134, "tuition": 63736}'::jsonb,'https://smu.edu/enrollmentservices/bursar/costofattendance','2026-10-14','high','Private university with a single tuition rate; the same printed figures are recorded in both in_state and out_of_state. ''Estimated Undergraduate Cost of Attendance for 2026-2027'', on-campus column, full-time fall and spring. ''Housing and food'' is printed as one combined line ($20,950), recorded under housing with food null. The indirect line ''Books, supplies, loan fees'' ($888) is a combined printed line recorded under books; it includes loan fees, which have no schema field.'),
  ('sc-229115','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": 4500, "housing": 7500, "personal": 2000, "total": 29783, "transportation": 2731, "tuition": 11852}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": 4500, "housing": 7500, "personal": 2000, "total": 42382, "transportation": 2731, "tuition": 24451}'::jsonb,'http://www.depts.ttu.edu/financialaid/costToAttend.php','2026-10-14','high','Official Financial Aid ''Cost to Attend'' page, 2026-2027 undergraduate tables. The page prints one combined ''TUITION & FEES'' line ($11,852 resident / $24,451 non-resident); recorded under tuition, fees null (not printed separately). ''MISCELLANEOUS'' recorded under personal. On Campus and Off Campus columns are identical for every line, so the budget is recorded as on-campus. The page also prints variant tables not used here: program/differential-rate tables (resident tuition & fees $13,604 and $13,658; non-resident $26,204 and $26,258), a bordering-county waiver table, an international-student table that adds a $2,930 health insurance line (non-resident total $42,581), and a living-at-home table (housing $3,538, transportation $900, miscellaneous $1,000).'),
  ('sc-230959','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 97386, "tuition": 72924, "fees": 542, "housing": 20920, "food": null, "books": 1000, "transportation": 1000, "personal": 1000}'::jsonb,'{"total": 97386, "tuition": 72924, "fees": 542, "housing": 20920, "food": null, "books": 1000, "transportation": 1000, "personal": 1000}'::jsonb,'https://www.middlebury.edu/student-financial-services/tuition-fees-and-payment/tuition-and-fees','2026-10-14','high','Student Financial Services cost-of-attendance chart for fall 2026 and spring 2027, full-time undergraduate student living on campus. Page prints a combined ''Living Expenses, including Housing (On-Campus) and Food (Meal Plan)'' line of $20,920, recorded under housing; food null. The fees field is the printed Student Activity Fee of $542. Direct costs (tuition, activity fee, housing and meal plan) subtotal $94,386 as printed. Single rate; same figures in both columns.'),
  ('sc-233921','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": null, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": null, "personal": null, "total": null, "transportation": null, "tuition": null}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1120, "fees": 3754, "food": 6826, "housing": 10394, "personal": 3150, "total": 64756, "transportation": 3014, "tuition": 36428}'::jsonb,'https://cnre.vt.edu/content/dam/finaid_vt_edu/Cost_of_Attendance/2627/UGNRON_UPDATED_05132026.pdf','2026-10-14','medium','Out-of-state on-campus budget is complete from Virginia Tech''s official 2026-2027 undergraduate COA document (updated 05/13/2026): Total Direct Cost $57,402 plus Total Indirect Costs $7,354 equals the printed Total Cost of Attendance $64,756. Books are printed as ''Course Materials'' ($1,120). Direct Loan Fees of $70 are printed within indirect costs and have no schema field. The same document notes a $2,150 computer budget item added for first-time students (freshman COA higher). The in-state on-campus budget document could not be retrieved by text fetch or search (only the in-state off-campus and out-of-state variants are indexed); in-state figures are left null rather than assembled from other-basis documents, and this side needs a browser pass to complete.'),
  ('sc-234076','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1540, "fees": 3940, "food": 7340, "housing": 8730, "personal": 3000, "total": 42014, "transportation": 550, "tuition": 16842}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1540, "fees": 4622, "food": 7340, "housing": 8730, "personal": 3000, "total": null, "transportation": null, "tuition": 57432}'::jsonb,'https://sfs.virginia.edu/financial-aid-new-applicants/financial-aid-basics/estimated-undergraduate-cost-attendance-2026-2027','2026-10-14','medium','UVA publishes its 2026-2027 cost of attendance by school of enrollment and year; figures recorded are the College of Arts & Sciences, First Year (the general undergraduate program). The page assumes a student living in Charlottesville/on-Grounds charged the full comprehensive fee, recorded as on-campus basis. Non-Virginian total is printed only as a range, $83,286 to $84,976, because the non-Virginian travel allowance is printed as a range ($550 to $2,240); per program rules the range is not recorded as a total, so out_of_state total and transportation are null. The ''Additional Categories'' subtotal folded into the printed totals also includes Direct loan fees of $72, which has no schema field. Student health insurance ($4,220/yr) is not included in the printed totals. Tuition and fees for other schools/years differ (e.g., Arts & Sciences third/fourth year tuition is $20,046 Virginian / $60,656 non-Virginian).'),
  ('sc-235316','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1188, "fees": 1120, "food": 8220, "housing": 8940, "personal": 1968, "total": 82689, "transportation": 2796, "tuition": 58390}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1188, "fees": 1120, "food": 8220, "housing": 8940, "personal": 1968, "total": 82689, "transportation": 2796, "tuition": 58390}'::jsonb,'https://www.gonzaga.edu/admission/tuition-scholarships-aid/financial-aid/cost-of-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Private university with a single tuition rate; the same printed figures are recorded in both in_state and out_of_state. Fees are printed as ''Required Fees'' ($1,120) and books as ''Books & Supplies'' ($1,188). Loan Fees of $67 are printed in the indirect costs and have no schema field. The same table prints an off-campus total of $83,787 and a with-family total of $74,973.'),
  ('sc-236948','2026-27','not-stated','{"books": 4482, "fees": 1676, "food": null, "housing": 18858, "personal": null, "total": 37680, "transportation": null, "tuition": 12664}'::jsonb,'{"books": 4482, "fees": 1676, "food": null, "housing": 18858, "personal": null, "total": 69596, "transportation": null, "tuition": 44580}'::jsonb,'https://uw-s3-cdn.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/162/2026/04/13125634/Preliminary-Cost-of-Attendance-for-the-2026-27-Academic-Year.pdf','2026-10-14','medium','Figures are the Seattle column of the UW Office of Planning & Budgeting document ''Preliminary 2026-27 Cost of Attendance for First-Year UW Undergraduates'' (the same document prints separate Bothell and Tacoma columns, not used here). ''Room & Board'' is a combined line ($18,858), recorded under housing; food null. ''Books, Personal, Transportation'' is a combined line ($4,482), recorded under books; personal and transportation null. Fees are the printed ''Annual Student Fees - Total'' ($1,676). A one-time New Student Enrollment & Orientation Fee of $467 (Seattle) is printed but is not included in the printed annual totals. The budget is stated for ''traditional undergraduates'' without an on/off-campus label, so basis is not-stated. The Office of Student Financial Aid student-budgets page (washington.edu/financialaid/gettingstarted/studentbudgets/) returned 404 when checked on 2026-10-14, and the document is labeled preliminary (its internal trend tables print different fee and tuition figures), so confidence is medium.'),
  ('sc-243744','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 97545, "tuition": 67731, "fees": 2610, "housing": 22944, "food": null, "books": 855, "transportation": null, "personal": 3405}'::jsonb,'{"total": 97545, "tuition": 67731, "fees": 2610, "housing": 22944, "food": null, "books": 855, "transportation": null, "personal": 3405}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.stanford.edu/undergrad/budget/index.html','2026-10-14','high','Full-time unmarried dependent undergraduate, Autumn/Winter/Spring. Same standard budget covers residence halls and off-campus living; on-campus selected. One price for all state residencies. Housing includes food; fees is Student Fees Allowance. Travel varies, so transportation is null. Numeric components reconcile exactly to printed $97,545; remainder $0. IMPORTANT: additional required first-year orientation $525 and document $250 fees are outside this table total; no revised fee subtotal or total is printed, so neither was calculated. Health insurance is also excluded: adequate coverage required; Cardinal Care may be waived with comparable coverage. No premium printed here. Fees allowance covers campus health, student activities, house dues, housing technology and course enrollment. Documented computer/medical costs may support individual budget increases. Gross cost before aid. Cloud browser verified the full 2026-27 table after fetch timed out; page update stamp March 3, 2026.'),
  ('sc-243780','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1090, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 16734, "personal": 2200, "total": 30586, "transportation": 570, "tuition": 9992}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1090, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 16734, "personal": 2200, "total": 49388, "transportation": 570, "tuition": 28794}'::jsonb,'https://www.purdue.edu/treasurer/finance/bursar-office/tuition/fee-rates-2026-2027/undergraduate-tuition-and-fees-2026-2027/','2026-10-14','high','Bursar''s 2026-2027 West Lafayette undergraduate flat-rate budget for the general program. The printed ''Sub-Total Tuition'' ($9,992 resident / $28,794 nonresident) combines the General Service charge ($9,718) with the Student Fitness and Wellness Fee ($234) and Student Activity Fee ($40); the nonresident figure adds Nonresident Tuition of $18,802. Recorded under tuition; fees null. ''Housing/Food'' is a combined printed line ($16,734), recorded under housing; food null. The printed ''Miscellaneous/Federal Student Loan Fees'' line ($2,200) is recorded under personal; the page notes loan fees apply only to federal loan borrowers. The page estimates on-campus and off-campus Housing/Food identically ($16,734); recorded as on-campus. Differential rates apply in some programs (Computer Science/Data Science & Engineering resident tuition subtotal $12,042, total $32,636; Daniels School of Business resident subtotal $11,428, total $32,022), Honors College adds $100 per semester, and international students add $3,310 tuition (base-program total $52,698); the base general-program budget is recorded.'),
  ('syracuse-university','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 95676, "tuition": 69180, "fees": 1869, "housing": 20580, "food": null, "books": 1847, "transportation": 839, "personal": 1294}'::jsonb,'{"total": 95676, "tuition": 69180, "fees": 1869, "housing": 20580, "food": null, "books": 1847, "transportation": 839, "personal": 1294}'::jsonb,'https://www.syracuse.edu/admissions-aid/cost/undergraduate-costs/','2026-10-14','high','Same published price for both residency categories, before aid. Housing combines housing and food (average); separate food not published. Printed total includes $67 loan fees if applicable; components plus loan fee sum exactly to $95,676. Mandatory health insurance $2,868 is additional unless waived for adequate private coverage; printed insured total $98,544. Off-campus total $93,398 ($96,266 insured); with-parents total $83,979 ($86,847 insured). Residential technology service fee mandatory with a university housing contract. First two years normally require university housing, with local-family commuter exception. Program/course fees may vary; page states upcoming-year figures remain estimates until May trustee approval.'),
  ('temple-university','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 48160, "tuition": 21474, "fees": null, "housing": 14084, "food": 5552, "books": 1330, "transportation": 2296, "personal": 3424}'::jsonb,'{"total": 64384, "tuition": 37698, "fees": null, "housing": 14084, "food": 5552, "books": 1330, "transportation": 2296, "personal": 3424}'::jsonb,'https://sfs.temple.edu/eligibility/your-financial-aid-offer/cost-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Selected the explicitly published College of Liberal Arts example for fall/spring 2026-27; tuition includes fees, with no separate fee amount in the COA table. Full-time undergraduate enrollment is 12-18 credits per semester. On-campus and off-campus budgets are identical. Housing is the median 2026-27 housing rate; food uses the J&H Unlimited plan. Commuter housing/meal allowance is $4,084, based on Premium 10. All selected components sum exactly to $48,160/$64,384; no unexplained remainder. No separately priced loan or insurance allowance appears in this table. These are anticipated institutional budgets, not individual bills. Tuition varies by academic college. Fox Business example: tuition/fees $26,322/$46,866 and total $53,008/$73,552, with identical remaining components. The linked master COA, updated July 10, 2026, corroborates the selected figures: https://sfs.temple.edu/sites/sfs/files/documents/2627%20Master%20UG%20COA.pdf. Other conventional-program annual totals (resident/nonresident) there: Boyer $50,800/$68,224; Film & Media and Klein $49,912/$66,184; Education, Social Work, Tyler-General and University College $48,160/$64,384; Engineering $52,648/$68,824; Public Health $52,000/$69,904; Science & Technology and Pharmacy B.S. $52,408/$68,632; Sport & Tourism $53,008/$71,128; Tyler-Fine Arts $55,144/$73,504; Tyler-Architecture $52,720/$69,736. Online Social Work/Fox BBA totals $45,520 for either residency assume 24 annual credits and are not selected. Source conflict: the separately labeled 2026-27 fact sheet still prints dorm/off-campus totals $42,884/$57,532, tuition/fees $20,195/$33,846, combined housing/meals $18,144, books $1,290, and combined travel/personal $3,255/$4,252; its commuter totals are $27,472/$42,120 with housing/meals $2,732. https://sfs.temple.edu/sites/sfs/files/documents/2026_27%20UG%20Fact%20Sheet.pdf. The 2026-27 Bulletin also retains that lower estimated component set at https://bulletin.temple.edu/undergraduate/cost-aid/. Selected the dedicated current COA page and matching July-updated master, preserving rather than blending conflicting estimates.'),
  ('umass-amherst','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": 8272, "housing": 9772, "personal": 1000, "total": 39896, "transportation": 400, "tuition": 19212}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1200, "fees": null, "food": 8272, "housing": 9772, "personal": 1000, "total": 63983, "transportation": 400, "tuition": 43299}'::jsonb,'https://www.umass.edu/financialaid/undergraduate-costs','2026-10-14','high','Full-time table, ''2026-2027 Costs (9-Month)''. The page prints a single combined ''Tuition & Fees'' line ($19,212 in-state / $43,299 out-of-state); that combined figure is recorded under tuition and fees is null because the page does not print them separately. Columns are headed ''On/Off Campus'' — the same budget applies to both, recorded as on-campus. Page states figures are estimates only, not final until approved by the UMass Board of Trustees. A New England Regional (NERSP) column is also printed (total $57,046). The page also prints an ''Average Federal Loan Fees'' line of $40 inside its indirect-cost subtotal; the schema has no field for it.'),
  ('university-of-arizona','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 600, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 17770, "personal": 2550, "total": 37270, "transportation": 2450, "tuition": 13900}'::jsonb,'{"books": 600, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 17770, "personal": 2550, "total": 67770, "transportation": 2450, "tuition": 44400}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.arizona.edu/cost/incoming','2026-10-14','high','2026-2027 Cost of Attendance for Incoming First-Year and Transfer students, on-campus budget. The page prints a combined ''Tuition & Fees'' line ($13,900 resident / $44,400 non-resident), recorded under tuition; fees null. It prints a combined ''Living Expenses - Housing & Food'' line ($17,770), recorded under housing; food null. ''Travel'' is recorded under transportation and ''Miscellaneous'' under personal. The page''s Federal Loan Fee and College Fees rows are blank/variable, with no schema field in any case. The page also publishes off-campus totals ($32,600 resident / $63,100 non-resident) and a living-with-parent budget; the on-campus budget is recorded.'),
  ('university-of-colorado-boulder','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 39992, "tuition": 15014, "fees": null, "housing": 20682, "food": null, "books": 1200, "transportation": 1314, "personal": 1782}'::jsonb,'{"total": 71784, "tuition": 46058, "fees": null, "housing": 20682, "food": null, "books": 1200, "transportation": 2062, "personal": 1782}'::jsonb,'https://www.colorado.edu/financialaid/cost/example-aid','2026-10-14','high','Published financial-aid budget for new full-time undergraduates, fall and spring, at the base tuition tier. Tuition includes combined tuition and fees; housing includes combined housing and food. Resident tuition assumes application for and authorization of the College Opportunity Fund. Program-specific tuition tiers differ. Excludes the one-time $232 new-student fee. Housing/food uses an average residence-hall room, 19 meals weekly and an additional food allowance; actual selections can cost less. Printed off-campus totals: resident $37,850; nonresident $69,642. Resident living-with-parents total: $30,990. Some nonresidents belonging to American Indian Tribes with historical Colorado ties may qualify for resident tuition. Both selected totals equal all printed budget components; no discrepancy.'),
  ('university-of-denver','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1000, "fees": 1584, "food": 7532, "housing": 11283, "personal": 1782, "total": 87581, "transportation": 627, "tuition": 63720}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1000, "fees": 1584, "food": 7532, "housing": 11283, "personal": 1782, "total": 87581, "transportation": 627, "tuition": 63720}'::jsonb,'https://www.du.edu/admission-aid/financial-aid-scholarships/undergraduate-financial-aid/price-and-affordability/cost-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Private university with a single tuition rate; the same printed figures are recorded in both in_state and out_of_state. 2026-2027 full-time budget for a student living on campus. Housing ($11,283) and food ($7,532) are printed as separate lines. The page also prints Loan Fees of $53, which has no schema field but is included in the printed Cost of Attendance total ($87,581). Per the page''s footnote, DU adds a $763 transportation allowance for non-Colorado residents (non-resident transportation $1,390; non-resident total $88,344); the base printed budget is recorded in both blocks per the single-rate convention.'),
  ('university-of-new-hampshire','2026-27','not-stated','{"books": 1000, "fees": 3868, "food": 5624, "housing": 9960, "personal": 3796, "total": 40920, "transportation": 300, "tuition": 16304}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1000, "fees": 3868, "food": 5624, "housing": 9960, "personal": 3796, "total": 62862, "transportation": 550, "tuition": 37996}'::jsonb,'https://www.unh.edu/financialaid/costs','2026-10-14','high','Table headed ''Durham Undergraduate Cost of Attendance 2026-2027''. The page does not state a housing basis (on-campus/off-campus/commuter) for this table, so basis is not-stated. ''Miscellaneous'' is recorded under personal. A $68 ''Loan Fee'' line is printed and is included in the page''s total; the schema has no field for it. A NE Regional column is also printed (total $53,298). Page footnote: costs are estimated and subject to change.'),
  ('university-of-oregon','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1434, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 18183, "personal": 2673, "total": 40236, "transportation": 471, "tuition": 17475}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1434, "fees": null, "food": null, "housing": 18183, "personal": 2673, "total": 71256, "transportation": 1500, "tuition": 47466}'::jsonb,'http://financialaid.uoregon.edu/cost_of_attendance','2026-10-14','high','UO Financial Aid & Scholarships ''Cost of Attendance'' page, current undergraduate table (2026-27; figures match the Oregon HECC 2026-27 Standard Student Budgets for the University of Oregon exactly, and the page''s $570 matriculation fee is the 2026-27 rate). Page prints a combined ''Tuition and Fees'' line, recorded under tuition; fees null. ''Living Expenses (On-Campus Housing and Food)'' is one combined line, recorded under housing; food null. Personal is the printed ''Miscellaneous Personal Expenses'' line. Budget is for new incoming undergraduates at 15 credits per term across three terms; the one-time $570 matriculation fee for entering students is excluded from the COA per the page.'),
  ('university-of-pennsylvania','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1412, "fees": 8308, "food": 6960, "housing": 13644, "personal": 2008, "total": 99082, "transportation": 1080, "tuition": 65670}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1412, "fees": 8308, "food": 6960, "housing": 13644, "personal": 2008, "total": 99082, "transportation": 1080, "tuition": 65670}'::jsonb,'https://srfs.upenn.edu/costs-budgeting/undergraduate-cost-attendance','2026-10-14','high','Private university; charges a single rate regardless of residency, so the same printed figures appear in both columns. Figures are Penn SRFS''s 2026-2027 ''Living On Campus'' undergraduate cost of attendance; total ($99,082) and all line items are printed and sum exactly. Penn also prints an off-campus total of $97,444 and a living-with-family total of $81,548. Books allowance variants printed on the page: $1,742 for first-year Nursing students; an average of $2,350 for Wharton students in years 2-4. Student health insurance and the New Student Orientation fee are not included in the total.'),
  ('university-of-rhode-island','2026-27','on-campus','{"total": 38936, "tuition": 15684, "fees": 2396, "housing": 16704, "food": null, "books": 1330, "transportation": 320, "personal": 2430}'::jsonb,'{"total": 61483, "tuition": 37350, "fees": 2396, "housing": 16704, "food": null, "books": 1330, "transportation": 1201, "personal": 2430}'::jsonb,'https://web.uri.edu/financial-aid/cost-of-attendance/','2026-10-14','high','2026-27 undergraduate on-campus institutional estimates before aid; housing includes food and is based on average housing costs. A separate $72 loan-origination allowance in each budget explains the difference between schema-component sums $38,864/$61,411 and printed COAs $38,936/$61,483. No unexplained remainder. Direct-cost subtotals $34,784/$56,450 are not full COA. Off-campus totals: $37,158/$60,516, housing/food $13,150, transportation $2,096/$3,788. Commuter totals: $34,662/$59,029, housing/food $3,750, transportation $9,000/$11,701. New England Regional tier has tuition $27,448, on-campus total $51,581, off-campus $50,614, commuter $49,127; eligibility must be established rather than assumed. COA page lists additional annual charges: AVS years 2-4 $1,482; Business $1,000; Engineering $1,500; Music years 2-4 $2,000; Music Therapy Clinical $3,300; Nursing years 2-4 $1,900; PharmD years 3-6 $7,000; Pharmaceutical Sciences years 3-4 $2,890; one-time new-student fee $300. Course/lab, document and parking charges can be additional. Published base totals exclude these extras. Supplemental 2026-27 full-time schedule, https://web.uri.edu/tuition-billing/tuition-and-fees/tuition-and-fees-full-time/, defines full time as 12-19 credits and prints estimated health insurance $3,512, assessed in fall and waivable for comparable coverage; it is excluded from the selected COAs. Required fees break down as registration $60, health services $646, technology $382, student services $1,308. The schedule marks the Business differential as applying to new Fall 2026 admits. Other applicable undergraduate fees: Landscape Architecture years 2-4 $236/semester; Biotech years 2-4 $500/semester; off-campus study $684/semester; one-time transcript $50 and document $115; course tiers $25/$55/$75; Music Therapy $1,650 per applicable course; Applied Music $500 for one credit or $1,000 for 2-4 credits; overload per credit beyond 19: resident $654, nonresident $1,556, regional $1,145. These are conditional/excluded extras, not replacements for the printed totals.'),
  ('university-of-utah','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1600, "fees": null, "food": 7898, "housing": 11300, "personal": 12000, "total": 45878, "transportation": 2600, "tuition": 10480}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1600, "fees": null, "food": 7898, "housing": 11300, "personal": 12000, "total": 68330, "transportation": 2600, "tuition": 32932}'::jsonb,'https://financialaid.utah.edu/tuition-and-fees/cost-of-attendance.php','2026-10-14','high','Page prints a combined ''Tuition & Fees'' line ($10,480 resident / $32,932 nonresident), recorded under tuition; fees null. Personal expenses are recorded exactly as printed ($12,000); the page''s footnote states loan fees are accounted for within the budget rather than itemized separately. A WUE (Western Undergraduate Exchange) total of $51,118 is also printed.'),
  ('university-of-vermont','2026-27','on-campus','{"books": 1320, "fees": 3058, "food": null, "housing": 14654, "personal": 2442, "total": 38762, "transportation": 234, "tuition": 16938}'::jsonb,'{"books": 1320, "fees": 3058, "food": null, "housing": 14654, "personal": 2443, "total": 68878, "transportation": 630, "tuition": 46655}'::jsonb,'https://www.uvm.edu/studentfinancialservices/costs-attending','2026-10-14','high','Tables headed ''On-Campus Vermont Resident Student'' and ''On-Campus Out-of-State Resident Student'' under ''Undergraduate Tuition and Fees, 2026-2027 Academic Year Costs'' (12-19 credit hours, two semesters), read on the start_url page (its cost tables sit in paged sections). Base columns used: Program Fee $0. Students in select colleges/schools (Nursing & Health Sciences, Grossman Business, Engineering & Mathematical Sciences) pay a $1,000 Program Fee; those columns total $39,762 in-state / $69,878 out-of-state. The page prints one combined ''Average Food and Housing'' line ($14,654); it is recorded under housing and food is null. fees is the printed Comprehensive Fee ($3,058); the page also prints a separate $30 Residential Engagement Council (REC) Fee, not folded into fees. ''Estimated Miscellaneous Personal Expenses'' is recorded under personal. The printed totals include an ''Estimated Loan Fees'' line ($86 in-state / $88 out-of-state); the schema has no field for it.')
